on (`strata help`).\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Changing\",\n      \"\",\n      \"- `strata edit MODULE <<'EOF' … EOF`: replaces or adds the definitions given, by name\",\n      \"  (always pipe them in: with nothing on stdin it opens $EDITOR and waits). Give a\",\n      \"  definition with its `///` doc lines, or they are dropped; `--rm NAME`\",\n      \"  deletes one. It is applied only if the whole codebase still checks.\",\n      \"- `strata rename OLD NEW`, `strata move NAME MODULE`: with every reference.\",\n      \"- `strata fix [NAME]`: makes the changes `check` and `edit` warn about (a contract\",\n      \"  that is a refinement: what one value is goes in its type, contracts relate values).\",\n      \"- An edit that breaks other code opens a pending change with holes (`?pending_N`):\",\n      \"  `strata status`, `strata holes`, then `strata done` or `strata abort`.\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Checking\",\n      \"\",\n      \"- `strata check`: types, exhaustive matches, refinements.\",\n      \"- `strata verify [SELECTOR]`: proves contracts (`requires`, `ensures`, `where`\",\n      \"  refinements, trait laws) with an SMT solver, runs counterexamples, fuzzes the rest.\",\n      \"  Verify what you changed, by name (`strata verify 'shop.total'`), not everything.\",\n      \"- `strata test [FILTER]`: the `test \\\"…\\\" { … }` blocks. `strata run [-- ARGS]`,\",\n      \"  `strata run FN ARGS`: run the program or one function. `strata build`: an executable\",\n      \"  (it verifies first: `--no-verify` for a throwaway build, such as a benchmark).\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## The language, roughly\",\n      \"\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"type Port = Int where it > 0 && it < 65536\",\n      \"type Shape = | Square(Int) | Rect { w: Int, h: Int }\",\n      \"\",\n      \"fn area(s: Shape) -> Int {\",\n      \"  match s {\",\n      \"    Square(side) => side * side,\",\n      \"    Rect { w, h } => w * h,\",\n      \"  }\",\n      \"}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"fn get(xs: List[Int], i: Natural) -> Int requires i < len(xs) = xs[i]\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"\",\n      \"`x := e` names a value, `mut x := e` a variable. Failures are values: a `Result` or\",\n      \"`Option`, passed up with `!` / `?` (no exceptions). What touches the outside world\",\n      \"(`Console`, `Disk`, `Process`) is a capability passed as a parameter, starting from\",\n      \"`main`'s. Prefer contracts and refinements proven by `verify` to example tests.\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Contracts: say what things mean\",\n      \"\",\n      \"A fact about one value is its type (`price: Cents where it >= 100`, `-> Natural`);\",\n      \"a contract (`requires`, `ensures`) relates values. For state behind a trait, give the\",\n      \"trait a `model` and write its contracts over it, instead of piling facts on each\",\n      \"function's inputs and outputs:\",\n      \"\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"trait Bounded {\",\n      \"  model items: List[Int]\",\n      \"  model room: Positive\",\n      \"  invariant len(self.items) <= self.room   // every value; each method keeps it\",\n      \"  ensures self.room == old self.room       // after every `mut self` method\",\n      \"\",\n      \"  fn size(self) -> Natural  ensures it == len(self.items)\",\n      \"  fn put(mut self, x: Int) -> Bool\",\n      \"    ensures it == (old len(self.items) < self.room)\",\n      \"    ensures self.items == if it { old self.items + [x] } else { old self.items }\",\n      \"}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"impl Bounded for Slots {\",\n      \"  model items = self.held\",\n      \"  model room = self.limit\",\n      \"  ...\",\n      \"}\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"\",\n      \"`verify` proves each `impl` against the model, and code taking a `Bounded` through\",\n      \"the model alone. Also: `law`s (a block of calls ending in a `Bool`), named results\",\n      \"(`-> (q: Natural, r: Natural)`), `shared trait` for state many workers use, and\",\n      \"`assumed` for a contract too costly to check at run time. Examples:\",\n      \"`examples/traits.strata`, `bank.strata`, `orders.strata` and `tasks/` at\",\n      \"github.com/anonx3247/strata.\",\n      \"\",\n    ],\n    \"\\n\",\n  )\n}","old_text":"/// The text of `SKILL.md`.\npub fn skill_text() -> String {\n  join(\n    [\n      \"---\",\n      \"name: strata\",\n      \"description: Read, change, check and verify Strata code (.strata files, strata.toml packages) through the `strata` command. Use whenever a task touches Strata code.\",\n      \"---\",\n      \"\",\n      \"# Strata\",\n      \"\",\n      \"Strata code is stored as its syntax tree: `.strata` files are binary. Never read or\",\n      \"write them directly (no cat, grep, sed or file-editing tools on them): go through\",\n      \"`strata`, which shows code as text and takes text back, checked. `strata help` lists\",\n      \"every command and its options; this is only a map.\",\n      \"\",\n      \"In a package (a folder with `strata.toml`) commands work on the package; for a\",\n      \"single file or another folder, put `--file PATH` before the command.\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Reading\",\n      \"\",\n      \"- `strata view`: the package's map, one line per definition.\",\n      \"- `strata view NAME --level 2`: definitions as source (`NAME`: a name, `prefix*`,\",\n      \"  `module:M`, `a,b`); `--level 1` their interfaces. `strata view MODULE`: a module as text.\",\n      \"- `strata find NAME`: where it is defined. `strata refs NAME`: where it is used.\",\n      \"- Builtins and std too: `strata view Dict`, `strata view insert` (every overload),\",\n      \"  `strata view std.json.parse` show their docs and signatures, also outside a package.\",\n      \"  A builtin's doc ends with its cost (`Cost: O(1) amortized, in place when ...`): read\",\n      \"  it instead of benchmarking. Where a value is copied instead of changed in place:\",\n      \"  the language docs' \\\"Values and copying\\\", and the `--copies` option (`strata help`).\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Changing\",\n      \"\",\n      \"- `strata edit MODULE <<'EOF' … EOF`: replaces or adds the definitions given, by name\",\n      \"  (always pipe them in: with nothing on stdin it opens $EDITOR and waits). Give a\",\n      \"  definition with its `///` doc lines, or they are dropped; `--rm NAME`\",\n      \"  deletes one. It is applied only if the whole codebase still checks.\",\n      \"- `strata rename OLD NEW`, `strata move NAME MODULE`: with every reference.\",\n      \"- `strata fix [NAME]`: makes the changes `check` and `edit` warn about (a contract\",\n      \"  that is a refinement: what one value is goes in its type, contracts relate values).\",\n      \"- An edit that breaks other code opens a pending change with holes (`?pending_N`):\",\n      \"  `strata status`, `strata holes`, then `strata done` or `strata abort`.\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Checking\",\n      \"\",\n      \"- `strata check`: types, exhaustive matches, refinements.\",\n      \"- `strata verify [SELECTOR]`: proves contracts (`requires`, `ensures`, `where`\",\n      \"  refinements, trait laws) with an SMT solver, runs counterexamples, fuzzes the rest.\",\n      \"  Verify what you changed, by name (`strata verify 'shop.total'`), not everything.\",\n      \"- `strata test [FILTER]`: the `test \\\"…\\\" { … }` blocks. `strata run [-- ARGS]`,\",\n      \"  `strata run FN ARGS`: run the program or one function. `strata build`: an executable\",\n      \"  (it verifies first: `--no-verify` for a throwaway build, such as a benchmark).\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## The language, roughly\",\n      \"\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"type Port = Int where it > 0 && it < 65536\",\n      \"type Shape = | Square(Int) | Rect { w: Int, h: Int }\",\n      \"\",\n      \"fn area(s: Shape) -> Int {\",\n      \"  match s {\",\n      \"    Square(side) => side * side,\",\n      \"    Rect { w, h } => w * h,\",\n      \"  }\",\n      \"}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"fn get(xs: List[Int], i: Int) -> Int requires i >= 0 && i < len(xs) = xs[i]\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"\",\n      \"`x := e` names a value, `mut x := e` a variable. Failures are values: a `Result` or\",\n      \"`Option`, passed up with `!` / `?` (no exceptions). What touches the outside world\",\n      \"(`Console`, `Disk`, `Process`) is a capability passed as a parameter, starting from\",\n      \"`main`'s. Prefer contracts and refinements proven by `verify` to example tests.\",\n      \"\",\n      \"## Contracts: say what things mean\",\n      \"\",\n      \"A fact about one value is its type (`price: Cents where it >= 100`, `-> Natural`);\",\n      \"a contract (`requires`, `ensures`) relates values. For state behind a trait, give the\",\n      \"trait a `model` and write its contracts over it, instead of piling facts on each\",\n      \"function's inputs and outputs:\",\n      \"\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"trait Bounded {\",\n      \"  model items: List[Int]\",\n      \"  model room: Positive\",\n      \"  invariant len(self.items) <= self.room   // every value; each method keeps it\",\n      \"  ensures self.room == old self.room       // after every `mut self` method\",\n      \"\",\n      \"  fn size(self) -> Natural  ensures it == len(self.items)\",\n      \"  fn put(mut self, x: Int) -> Bool\",\n      \"    ensures it == (old len(self.items) < self.room)\",\n      \"    ensures self.items == if it { old self.items + [x] } else { old self.items }\",\n      \"}\",\n      \"\",\n      \"impl Bounded for Slots {\",\n      \"  model items = self.held\",\n      \"  model room = self.limit\",\n      \"  ...\",\n      \"}\",\n      \"```\",\n      \"\",\n      \"`verify` proves each `impl` against the model, and code taking a `Bounded` through\",\n      \"the model alone. Also: `law`s (a block of calls ending in a `Bool`), named results\",\n      \"(`-> (q: Natural, r: Natural)`), `shared trait` for state many workers use, and\",\n      \"`assumed` for a contract too costly to check at run time. Examples:\",\n      \"`examples/traits.strata`, `bank.strata`, `orders.strata` and `tasks/` at\",\n      \"github.com/anonx3247/strata.\",\n      \"\",\n    ],\n    \"\\n\",\n  )\n}"}]}
{"id":"f41273c55a53a9bd","time":1795656210,"message":"fix check.untyped_result, codegen.calls_in, codegen.all_small, codegen.known, codegen.conversion_name, codegen.in_place_field, deps.before, eval.call_method, eval.bool_of, eval.element_lambda, graph.all_entries, comptime_stamp, solver_of, smt.not_modelled, smt.type_pattern, smt.apply_ctor","changes":[{"name":"check.untyped_result","kind":"fn","old":"16438fc86368f052","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"check","old_text":"/// A tagged call whose type isn't fully known, marked so that a function's\n/// declared result can still be given to it in tail position.\nfn untyped_result(call: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  ast.Block {\n    stmts: [ast.Let { pat: ast.Bind(\"$result\"), ty: None, value: call }],\n    last: ast.Var(\"$result\"),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"codegen.calls_in","kind":"fn","old":"b9766171e4a21aec","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","old_text":"/// The functions an expression calls by name.\nfn calls_in(e: ast.Expr) -> List[String] {\n  mut out := match e {\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(n), .. } => [n],\n    _ => [],\n  }\n  for c in codegen.sub_exprs(e) {\n    out += codegen.calls_in(c)\n  }\n  out\n}"},{"name":"codegen.all_small","kind":"fn","old":"fb9977f7e56e9794","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","old_text":"/// Whether every `Int` is small: in [-2^62, 2^62), so its two top bits are\n/// equal.\nfn all_small(mut g: codegen.Gen, xs: List[String]) -> String {\n  mut acc := \"\"\n  for x in xs {\n    (sh, xo) := (codegen.fresh(mut g, \"sh\"), codegen.fresh(mut g, \"xo\"))\n    codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{sh} = shl i64 {x}, 1\")\n    codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{xo} = xor i64 {x}, {sh}\")\n    acc = if acc == \"\" {\n      xo\n    } else {\n      o := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"or\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{o} = or i64 {acc}, {xo}\")\n      o\n    }\n  }\n  r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"small\")\n  codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = icmp sge i64 {acc}, 0\")\n  r\n}"},{"name":"codegen.known","kind":"fn","old":"8b5af84635a7de37","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","old_text":"/// Whether a type is fully known.\nfn known(t: check.Ty) -> Bool {\n  match t {\n    check.TAny | check.TGen(_) => false,\n    check.TList(a) => codegen.known(a),\n    check.TNamed { args, .. } => args.all(a -> codegen.known(a)),\n    check.TFn { params, ret } => params.all(a -> codegen.known(a)) && codegen.known(ret),\n    _ => true,\n  }\n}"},{"name":"codegen.conversion_name","kind":"fn","old":"fcbeb3a41aa8e2e5","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","old_text":"/// Whether `name` is a sized integer conversion (`to_int`, `to_u32`,\n/// `wrap_u32`).\nfn conversion_name(name: String) -> Bool {\n  if name == \"to_int\" {\n    return true\n  }\n  for w in [\"i8\", \"i16\", \"i32\", \"i64\", \"u8\", \"u16\", \"u32\", \"u64\"] {\n    if name == \"to_\" + w || name == \"wrap_\" + w {\n      return true\n    }\n  }\n  false\n}"},{"name":"codegen.in_place_field","kind":"fn","old":"8d05b11dbb93aee4","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","old_text":"/// Whether `x.f = v` can change `x`'s value in place when nothing else\n/// holds it. True for a tuple, or a record with one constructor that is not\n/// `distinct` and has no refinement of its own, when `x` was not declared\n/// with a refined type.\nfn in_place_field(\n  g: codegen.Gen,\n  l: codegen.Local,\n  t: check.Ty,\n  f: String,\n) -> Bool {\n  if contains(g.declared, l.slot) || codegen.boxed(g, t) {\n    return false\n  }\n  match t {\n    check.TNamed { name, .. } => codegen.field_index(g, t, f).0 >= 0\n      && !contains(g.distincts, name)\n      && !contains(g.refines, name),\n    _ => false,\n  }\n}"},{"name":"deps.before","kind":"fn","old":"42e1aeb89ab6c739","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"deps","old_text":"/// By code point.\nfn before(a: String, b: String) -> Bool {\n  xs := chars(a)\n  ys := chars(b)\n  for i in 0..len(xs) {\n    if i >= len(ys) {\n      return false\n    }\n    x := ord(get(xs, i) ?? \"\")\n    y := ord(get(ys, i) ?? \"\")\n    if x != y {\n      return x < y\n    }\n  }\n  len(xs) < len(ys)\n}"},{"name":"eval.call_method","kind":"fn","old":"72acc7e43da8a11b","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"eval","old_text":"/// `v.m(args)` for a method of `v`'s type.\nfn call_method(\n  mut st: eval.State,\n  w: eval.World,\n  v: ast.Expr,\n  m: String,\n  args: List[ast.Expr],\n) -> Result[ast.Expr, eval.Escape] {\n  match eval.method_of(w, v, m) {\n    Some(c) => Ok(eval.call(mut st, w, c, [v] + args)!.0),\n    None => Err(\n      eval.runtime(\n        eval.head_of(w, v) + \" has no method `\" + m + \"`\",\n      ),\n    ),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"eval.bool_of","kind":"fn","old":"34c7cfd133abdfdd","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"eval","old_text":"fn bool_of(v: ast.Expr) -> Bool {\n  v == ast.BoolLit(true)\n}"},{"name":"eval.element_lambda","kind":"fn","old":"14d8d41468dc30a0","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"eval","old_text":"/// A lambda taking `params`, then an element matched against `pat`.\nfn element_lambda(\n  params: List[ast.LamParam],\n  pat: ast.Pattern,\n  body: ast.Expr,\n) -> ast.Expr {\n  match pat {\n    ast.Bind(x) => ast.Lambda {\n      params: params + [ast.LamParam { name: x, ty: None }],\n      body,\n    },\n    _ => ast.Lambda {\n      params: params + [ast.LamParam { name: \"$item\", ty: None }],\n      body: ast.Block {\n        stmts: [ast.Let { pat, ty: None, value: ast.Var(\"$item\") }],\n        last: body,\n      },\n    },\n  }\n}"},{"name":"graph.all_entries","kind":"fn","old":"841f242134aa3fd1","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"graph","old_text":"/// Every entry, with `verdict`, by `label` at `place`.\nfn all_entries(\n  s: graph.Subject,\n  label: String,\n  place: String,\n  verdict: String,\n) -> List[graph.Edge] {\n  s.variants.map(\n    b -> graph.Edge { from: \"\", to: b, by: label, verdict, place },\n  )\n}"},{"name":"comptime_stamp","kind":"fn","old":"ab200884e6dae753","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"","old_text":"/// What every compile-time value's key starts with: core's and the\n/// prelude's code, which every compile has. `\"\"` when nothing is cached\n/// (`caching`). The compiler's identity is left out: a value is pure and\n/// deterministic, so it depends only on the code it runs, and a new\n/// compiler reads the values an earlier one computed.\nfn comptime_stamp(disk: std.fs.Disk) -> String {\n  if !cache.caching() {\n    \"\"\n  } else {\n    std_fingerprint(disk, core_files() + [\"runtime/prelude.strata\"])\n  }\n}"},{"name":"solver_of","kind":"fn","old":"9f78de5e5f59c608","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"","old_text":"/// `STRATA_SOLVER`, else the z3 a release ships beside the executable\n/// (`bin/strata` → `lib/strata/z3`), else `z3` on the PATH.\nfn solver_of(disk: std.fs.Disk, process: std.process.Process) -> String {\n  match process.var(\"STRATA_SOLVER\") {\n    Some(s) => s,\n    None => {\n      shipped := toolchain_exe_dir() + \"/../lib/strata/z3\"\n      if toolchain_exe_dir() != \"\" && disk.exists(shipped) {\n        shipped\n      } else {\n        \"z3\"\n      }\n    },\n  }\n}"},{"name":"smt.not_modelled","kind":"fn","old":"1369f1e66e2efb37","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"smt","old_text":"/// The name of an expression kind, for a message saying it is not\n/// modelled.\nfn not_modelled(e: ast.Expr) -> String {\n  match e {\n    ast.TupleExpr(_) => \"tuples\",\n    ast.ListExpr(_) => \"lists\",\n    ast.CtorExpr { .. } => \"constructors\",\n    ast.FieldOf { .. } => \"fields\",\n    ast.Lambda { .. } => \"lambdas\",\n    ast.IsExpr { .. } => \"`is`\",\n    ast.MatchExpr { .. } => \"`match`\",\n    ast.Try { .. } => \"`!` and `?`\",\n    ast.Except { .. } => \"`except`\",\n    ast.Fallback { .. } => \"`??`\",\n    _ => \"this expression\",\n  }\n}"},{"name":"smt.type_pattern","kind":"fn","old":"c83a360c40aaaa75","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"smt","old_text":"/// Whether a pattern names a type (`Positive =>`) instead of a\n/// constructor.\nfn type_pattern(vc: smt.Vc, p: ast.Pattern) -> Bool {\n  match p {\n    ast.CtorPattern { name, args: ast.NoPats } => !contains(vc.ctors, name) && smt.is_type_name(vc, name),\n    ast.CtorPattern { name, args: ast.TypePats(_) } => smt.is_type_name(vc, name),\n    _ => false,\n  }\n}"},{"name":"smt.apply_ctor","kind":"fn","old":"0a4a725592f57e2c","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"smt","old_text":"/// Constructor `c` applied to the terms of `xs`, of types `tys`.\nfn apply_ctor(\n  mut vc: smt.Vc,\n  c: String,\n  tys: List[ast.TypeExpr],\n  xs: List[smt.Val],\n) -> Option[String] {\n  if len(xs) == 0 {\n    return Some(smt.sym(c))\n  }\n  mut ts := []\n  for (k, x) in enumerate(xs) {\n    mut ts.push(smt.pure_term(mut vc, get(tys, k) ?? ast.UnitType, x)?)\n  }\n  Some(\"(\" + smt.sym(c) + \" \" + join(ts, \" \") + \")\")\n}"}],"fixed":["check.untyped_result","codegen.calls_in","codegen.all_small","codegen.known","codegen.conversion_name","codegen.in_place_field","deps.before","eval.call_method","eval.bool_of","eval.element_lambda","graph.all_entries","comptime_stamp","solver_of","smt.not_modelled","smt.type_pattern","smt.apply_ctor"]}
{"id":"942c797841d80897","time":1795656564,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"check.Inf","kind":"type","old":"c4539e5aff4a4ae8","new":"6ac8287c131ac814","interface_changed":true,"affected":["check.fresh","check.resolve","check.res","check.unify","check.error","check.expect","check.join_union","check.numeric","check.fresh_for","check.place","check.bind_typed","check.infer_all","check.binary","check.infer_block","check.infer_call","check.infer_if","check.infer_list","check.infer_match","check.infer_ctor","check.infer_lambda","check.infer","check.infer_method","check.var_type","check.is_sum","check.fresh_scheme","check.builtin_call","check.fits_all","check.element_of","check.fits","check.arm_variants","check.implements","check.bound_method","check.program_type","check.static_call","check.arm_members","check.as_trait","check.trait_method","check.fn_inferred","check.annotated","check.next_let","check.fill","check.wrong_try","check.not_result","check.not_iterable","check.check_spec","check.early_error","check.awaited","check.not_awaitable","check.outside_scope","check.own_trait_of","check.trait_fn","check.reaches","check.solve_pending","check.holds_sender","check.written_calls","check.infer_untagged","check.sized_expected","check.int_literal","check.sized_operands","check.task_body","check.fill_arms","check.lam_unmarked","check.holes_found","check.code_trait_method","check.default_errors","check.owned_reads","check.traits_declaring","check.implements_trait","check.ambiguity","check.self_args","check.named_refinement","check.excluded_by","check.ctor_fields","check.member_for","check.cover_of","check.atoms","check.covers","check.missing","check.useful","check.check_coverage","check.type_of_column","check.mut_narrower","check.written_cover","check.refinement_within","check.code_method_problem","check.unmet_bound","check.iter_builtin","check.own_calls","check.trait_fn_of","check.element_assigned","check.listed_arg","check.as_listed","check.listed_args","check.string_method","check.tuple_taken_apart","check.lam_written","check.unused_values","check.changing_call","check.allocating_arith","check.noalloc_typed","check.spread_calls","check.spread_error","check.infer_spread","check.spread_fn_params","check.spread_method_params","check.spread_method_of","check.spread_filled","check.dropped_results","check.trait_with_method","check.provided_method","check.read_owners","check.named_types","check.fn_errors","check.instantiated","check.fn_lambdas_typed","check.holes_of","check.mark_field_reads","check.own_methods_resolved","check.typed_one","check.decl_type_errors","check.spread_body","check.field_reads","eval_files","instantiated_files","check.lambdas_typed","holes_command","check_summary","finding.uses_of","rename_command","verified_decls","check.typed","check.type_errors_with","check.spreads_resolved","unused.members","command_line","check_command","finding.uses_from","finding.used_by_tree","finding.refs_command","verified_with","static_graph","codegen.new_gen","computed_value","repl_eval","check.type_errors","check_errors_in","literal_errors","expanded","unused.findings","main","strata_command","finding.uses_tree","verified_program","verify_file","build_command","graph_command","graph_diff","codegen.generate","codegen.read_back","comptime_value","repl_command","check_errors_with","edit_errors","literal_errors_of","codegen_with","with_base","unused_of","edit_unused","core_unused","codegen.entry","codegen.compiled_alone","eval.run","smt_file","termination_file","verify_command","build_proofs","alongside_command","search_invariants","diff_command","core_rt_text","comptime_values","loaded_errors","check_errors_of","edit_file","file_errors","apply_change","apply_edit","codegen_text","compiled_drivers","compiling","replay_all","test_command","std_library","built_ir","core_rt_object","run_command","fix_loops","build_core_command","comptime_runner","package_errors","merge_file_command","merged_checks","call_command","edit_command","check_files","move_command","fix_command","edit_in_editor","codegen_file","jit_file","fuzz_file","graph_runs","replay","or_solver_inputs","program_objects","sync_command","check_fn","linked"],"module":"check","text":"/// The inference's state: what type variables stand for, the next fresh\n/// one, the errors found, the program's functions, and the return type of\n/// the function being checked.\ntype Inf = {\n  subst: Dict[Int, check.Ty],\n  next: Int,\n  errs: List[String],\n  fns: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  ret: check.Ty,\n  types: check.Types,\n  tparams: Set[String],\n  // the traits each type parameter in scope is bound by\n  tbounds: Dict[String, List[String]],\n  methods: check.Methods,\n  narrowed: Set[String],\n  // the variables an arm assigns to: their declared types there\n  exempt: Set[String],\n  // the variables declared outside the innermost `scope` (None: in none)\n  outside: Option[Set[String]],\n  // the variables from outside the closure or `spawn` being checked\n  captured: Set[String],\n  builtins: Dict[String, List[check.Builtin]],\n  // each variable declared (`x := e`, `mut x := e`) and the type it got, in\n  // the order met; `typed` writes them into the tree\n  lets: List[(String, check.Ty)],\n  // each lambda parameter marked by `lambdas_typed` (`$lam…`) and the type\n  // it got\n  lambdas: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  // the trait obligations met (a trait's method used as a function: its\n  // `Self`, the trait, the method), solved once the body is checked\n  pending: List[(check.Ty, String, String)],\n  // the type of each call tagged by `instantiated` (`f#3(..)`, `x.m#4(..)`)\n  insts: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  // each arithmetic operation met (`+`, `-`, ...) and its type. On `Int`,\n  // `String` or `List` it allocates, which `noalloc` code can't do.\n  arith: List[(String, check.Ty)],\n  // each hole met (`?name`): the type it must have, and the variables in\n  // scope there with their types (`strata holes`)\n  holes: List[(String, check.Ty, Dict[String, check.Ty])] = [],\n  // each variable's type as written, when refined (`n: Positive`, or the\n  // refinement an arm named: `Positive => …`); a match on it may leave out\n  // what the refinement excludes\n  written: Dict[String, ast.TypeExpr] = Dict[String, ast.TypeExpr] {},\n  // each argument that is a finite iterator where its parameter is a `List`\n  // (the callee's name, the argument's index, the argument); `as_listed`\n  // converts them with `to_list`\n  as_lists: List[(String, Int, ast.Expr)] = [],\n  // each expression statement met, its type, and the type of the variable\n  // its call's first argument names (`xs` in `push(xs, 1)`), if any. A\n  // value other than `()` is an error once the body is solved (`unused_values`).\n  discarded: List[(ast.Expr, check.Ty, Option[check.Ty])] = [],\n  // each call spreading records (`f(...x)`, tagged `f#s0_1` by\n  // `spread_bound`), written out (`f(x.a, x.b)`), by its tag\n  spreads: Dict[String, ast.Expr] = Dict[String, ast.Expr] {},\n  // the errors of calls spreading records, also in `errs`\n  spread_errs: List[String] = [],\n  // the type of what each `for` runs over; a `noalloc` function can't run\n  // over what needs a list made (`noalloc_typed`)\n  iters: List[check.Ty] = [],\n  // each method called and its receiver's type, for `noalloc_typed`\n  recvs: List[(String, check.Ty)] = [],\n  // each `_ := e` met and the type of `e`; a `Result` thrown away this way\n  // is a warning (`dropped_results`)\n  dropped: List[(ast.Expr, check.Ty)] = [],\n}","old_text":"/// The inference's state: what type variables stand for, the next fresh\n/// one, the errors found, the program's functions, and the return type of\n/// the function being checked.\ntype Inf = {\n  subst: Dict[Int, check.Ty],\n  next: Int,\n  errs: List[String],\n  fns: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  ret: check.Ty,\n  types: check.Types,\n  tparams: Set[String],\n  // the traits each type parameter in scope is bound by\n  tbounds: Dict[String, List[String]],\n  methods: check.Methods,\n  narrowed: Set[String],\n  // the variables tested with `is`\n  tested: Set[String],\n  // the variables an arm assigns to: their declared types there\n  exempt: Set[String],\n  // the variables declared outside the innermost `scope` (None: in none)\n  outside: Option[Set[String]],\n  // the variables from outside the closure or `spawn` being checked\n  captured: Set[String],\n  builtins: Dict[String, List[check.Builtin]],\n  // each variable declared (`x := e`, `mut x := e`) and the type it got, in\n  // the order met; `typed` writes them into the tree\n  lets: List[(String, check.Ty)],\n  // each lambda parameter marked by `lambdas_typed` (`$lam…`) and the type\n  // it got\n  lambdas: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  // the trait obligations met (a trait's method used as a function: its\n  // `Self`, the trait, the method), solved once the body is checked\n  pending: List[(check.Ty, String, String)],\n  // the type of each call tagged by `instantiated` (`f#3(..)`, `x.m#4(..)`)\n  insts: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  // each arithmetic operation met (`+`, `-`, ...) and its type. On `Int`,\n  // `String` or `List` it allocates, which `noalloc` code can't do.\n  arith: List[(String, check.Ty)],\n  // each hole met (`?name`): the type it must have, and the variables in\n  // scope there with their types (`strata holes`)\n  holes: List[(String, check.Ty, Dict[String, check.Ty])] = [],\n  // each variable's type as written, when refined (`n: Positive`, or the\n  // refinement an arm named: `Positive => …`); a match on it may leave out\n  // what the refinement excludes\n  written: Dict[String, ast.TypeExpr] = Dict[String, ast.TypeExpr] {},\n  // each argument that is a finite iterator where its parameter is a `List`\n  // (the callee's name, the argument's index, the argument); `as_listed`\n  // converts them with `to_list`\n  as_lists: List[(String, Int, ast.Expr)] = [],\n  // each expression statement met, its type, and the type of the variable\n  // its call's first argument names (`xs` in `push(xs, 1)`), if any. A\n  // value other than `()` is an error once the body is solved (`unused_values`).\n  discarded: List[(ast.Expr, check.Ty, Option[check.Ty])] = [],\n  // each call spreading records (`f(...x)`, tagged `f#s0_1` by\n  // `spread_bound`), written out (`f(x.a, x.b)`), by its tag\n  spreads: Dict[String, ast.Expr] = Dict[String, ast.Expr] {},\n  // the errors of calls spreading records, also in `errs`\n  spread_errs: List[String] = [],\n  // the type of what each `for` runs over; a `noalloc` function can't run\n  // over what needs a list made (`noalloc_typed`)\n  iters: List[check.Ty] = [],\n  // each method called and its receiver's type, for `noalloc_typed`\n  recvs: List[(String, check.Ty)] = [],\n  // each `_ := e` met and the type of `e`; a `Result` thrown away this way\n  // is a warning (`dropped_results`)\n  dropped: List[(ast.Expr, check.Ty)] = [],\n}"},{"name":"check.fn_inferred","kind":"fn","old":"12ab9f59531c3d85","new":"84846cdaf6b031a0","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"check","text":"/// The inference's state after checking `f`'s body.\nfn fn_inferred(\n  f: ast.FnDecl,\n  tps: Set[String],\n  types: check.Types,\n  fns: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  methods: check.Methods,\n  builtins: Dict[String, List[check.Builtin]],\n) -> check.Inf {\n  // a test's body has no function to return from (`outside_fn`)\n  ret := match f.ret {\n    ast.Named { name: \"$outside\", .. } => check.TNamed { name: \"$outside\", args: [] },\n    _ => check.lower(types, tps, f.ret),\n  }\n  mut i := check.Inf {\n    subst: Dict[Int, check.Ty] {},\n    next: 0,\n    errs: [],\n    fns,\n    ret,\n    types,\n    tparams: tps,\n    tbounds: check.bounds_by_param(f.bounds),\n    methods,\n    narrowed: check.narrowed_in(f.body, Set[String] {}),\n    exempt: Set[String] {},\n    outside: None,\n    captured: Set[String] {},\n    builtins,\n    lets: [],\n    lambdas: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n    pending: [],\n    insts: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n    arith: [],\n  }\n  mut env := Dict[String, check.Ty] {}\n  for p in f.params {\n    match p.ty {\n      ast.Named { args: [], .. } | ast.Named { name: \"NonEmpty\", .. } | ast.Refined { .. } => mut i.written.insert(p.name, p.ty),\n      _ => (),\n    }\n    // a `comptime` parameter is worked on while compiling (`f.default_value`\n    // is the field's default, written out by `derive`): not modelled\n    mut env.insert(\n      p.name,\n      if p.compile_time {\n        check.TAny\n      } else {\n        check.lower(types, tps, p.ty)\n      },\n    )\n  }\n  bt := check.infer(mut i, f.body, env, if check.outside_fn(ret) {\n    None\n  } else {\n    Some(ret)\n  })\n  if !check.outside_fn(ret) {\n    check.expect(mut i, ret, bt, \"function body\")\n  }\n  check.solve_pending(mut i)\n  // an unused value is reported once the body has no other error: an\n  // expression that doesn't check is no value to keep\n  if i.errs == [] {\n    check.unused_values(mut i)\n  }\n  i\n}","old_text":"/// The inference's state after checking `f`'s body.\nfn fn_inferred(\n  f: ast.FnDecl,\n  tps: Set[String],\n  types: check.Types,\n  fns: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  methods: check.Methods,\n  builtins: Dict[String, List[check.Builtin]],\n) -> check.Inf {\n  // a test's body has no function to return from (`outside_fn`)\n  ret := match f.ret {\n    ast.Named { name: \"$outside\", .. } => check.TNamed { name: \"$outside\", args: [] },\n    _ => check.lower(types, tps, f.ret),\n  }\n  mut i := check.Inf {\n    subst: Dict[Int, check.Ty] {},\n    next: 0,\n    errs: [],\n    fns,\n    ret,\n    types,\n    tparams: tps,\n    tbounds: check.bounds_by_param(f.bounds),\n    methods,\n    narrowed: check.narrowed_in(f.body, Set[String] {}),\n    tested: check.tested_in(f.body, Set[String] {}),\n    exempt: Set[String] {},\n    outside: None,\n    captured: Set[String] {},\n    builtins,\n    lets: [],\n    lambdas: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n    pending: [],\n    insts: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n    arith: [],\n  }\n  mut env := Dict[String, check.Ty] {}\n  for p in f.params {\n    match p.ty {\n      ast.Named { args: [], .. } | ast.Named { name: \"NonEmpty\", .. } | ast.Refined { .. } => mut i.written.insert(p.name, p.ty),\n      _ => (),\n    }\n    // a `comptime` parameter is worked on while compiling (`f.default_value`\n    // is the field's default, written out by `derive`): not modelled\n    mut env.insert(\n      p.name,\n      if p.compile_time {\n        check.TAny\n      } else {\n        check.lower(types, tps, p.ty)\n      },\n    )\n  }\n  bt := check.infer(mut i, f.body, env, if check.outside_fn(ret) {\n    None\n  } else {\n    Some(ret)\n  })\n  if !check.outside_fn(ret) {\n    check.expect(mut i, ret, bt, \"function body\")\n  }\n  check.solve_pending(mut i)\n  // an unused value is reported once the body has no other error: an\n  // expression that doesn't check is no value to keep\n  if i.errs == [] {\n    check.unused_values(mut i)\n  }\n  i\n}"},{"name":"check.default_errors","kind":"fn","old":"cd19bf1345528fcf","new":"559b9486a42bc9ef","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"check","text":"/// The errors of fields' defaults. Each must have its field's type, checked\n/// where the type is defined with nothing in scope.\nfn default_errors(\n  fs: List[ast.Field],\n  tps: Set[String],\n  types: check.Types,\n  fns: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  methods: check.Methods,\n  builtins: Dict[String, List[check.Builtin]],\n) -> List[String] {\n  mut out := []\n  for f in fs {\n    match f.default {\n      Some(x) => {\n        want := check.lower(types, tps, f.ty)\n        mut i := check.Inf {\n          subst: Dict[Int, check.Ty] {},\n          next: 0,\n          errs: [],\n          fns,\n          ret: check.TAny,\n          types,\n          tparams: tps,\n          tbounds: Dict[String, List[String]] {},\n          methods,\n          narrowed: Set[String] {},\n          exempt: Set[String] {},\n          outside: None,\n          captured: Set[String] {},\n          builtins,\n          lets: [],\n          lambdas: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n          pending: [],\n          insts: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n          arith: [],\n        }\n        got := check.infer(mut i, x, Dict[String, check.Ty] {}, Some(want))\n        check.expect(\n          mut i,\n          want,\n          got,\n          \"default of field `\" + f.name + \"`\",\n        )\n        check.solve_pending(mut i)\n        out += i.errs\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}","old_text":"/// The errors of fields' defaults. Each must have its field's type, checked\n/// where the type is defined with nothing in scope.\nfn default_errors(\n  fs: List[ast.Field],\n  tps: Set[String],\n  types: check.Types,\n  fns: Dict[String, check.Ty],\n  methods: check.Methods,\n  builtins: Dict[String, List[check.Builtin]],\n) -> List[String] {\n  mut out := []\n  for f in fs {\n    match f.default {\n      Some(x) => {\n        want := check.lower(types, tps, f.ty)\n        mut i := check.Inf {\n          subst: Dict[Int, check.Ty] {},\n          next: 0,\n          errs: [],\n          fns,\n          ret: check.TAny,\n          types,\n          tparams: tps,\n          tbounds: Dict[String, List[String]] {},\n          methods,\n          narrowed: Set[String] {},\n          tested: Set[String] {},\n          exempt: Set[String] {},\n          outside: None,\n          captured: Set[String] {},\n          builtins,\n          lets: [],\n          lambdas: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n          pending: [],\n          insts: Dict[String, check.Ty] {},\n          arith: [],\n        }\n        got := check.infer(mut i, x, Dict[String, check.Ty] {}, Some(want))\n        check.expect(\n          mut i,\n          want,\n          got,\n          \"default of field `\" + f.name + \"`\",\n        )\n        check.solve_pending(mut i)\n        out += i.errs\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}"}]}
{"id":"e2247d1145e58b0d","time":1795656600,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"EditScope","kind":"type","old":"6b45b1154d98215b","new":"e967459323dedbea","interface_changed":true,"affected":["edit_scope","edit_errors","apply_change","apply_edit","rename_command","move_command","fix_command","edit_command","edit_in_editor","command_line","repl_command","main","strata_command","codegen.entry","codegen.generate","codegen.new_gen","codegen.compiled_alone","eval.run","codegen_with","core_rt_text","computed_value","repl_eval","codegen.read_back","eval_files","codegen_text","literal_errors","compiled_drivers","compiling","replay_all","test_command","std_library","built_ir","core_rt_object","build_core_command","comptime_value","codegen_file","jit_file","fuzz_file","alongside_command","literal_errors_of","verify_file","graph_runs","replay","or_solver_inputs","check_command","verify_command","build_command","run_command","static_graph","program_objects","comptime_values","call_command","loaded_errors","edit_file","file_errors","build_proofs","search_invariants","check_fn","graph_command","graph_diff","linked","expanded","comptime_runner","package_errors","check_files","fix_loops","diff_command","with_base"],"module":"","text":"/// What an edit from one version of a package to the next can affect:\n/// - `changed`: the definitions it changed or added\n/// - `checked`: the definitions to check: those changed, and the users of\n/// one whose interface changed or that was removed\n/// - `graph`: each definition's dependencies, as module headers list them,\n/// found again for the changed ones\ntype EditScope = {\n  changed: Set[String],\n  checked: Set[String],\n  graph: Dict[String, List[String]],\n}","old_text":"/// What an edit from one version of a package to the next can affect:\n/// - `changed`: the definitions it changed or added\n/// - the definitions it removed, by qualified name\n/// - `checked`: the definitions to check: those changed, and the users of\n/// one whose interface changed or that was removed\n/// - `graph`: each definition's dependencies, as module headers list them,\n/// found again for the changed ones\ntype EditScope = {\n  changed: Set[String],\n  removed: List[String],\n  checked: Set[String],\n  graph: Dict[String, List[String]],\n}"},{"name":"edit_scope","kind":"fn","old":"c594b9ecf77eb02c","new":"b4cf2bd5139e6626","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"","text":"/// `files` is the package's module files before the edit (path, bytes). A\n/// body change can't break other definitions: only a changed interface or\n/// a removed definition has its users checked. Users are found through the\n/// dependencies module headers list, and, for what headers don't list (a\n/// method called on a value, a field read), through the names in their\n/// string tables.\nfn edit_scope(\n  old: List[ast.Decl],\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  files: List[(String, List[Int])],\n  global: Bool,\n) -> EditScope {\n  mut before := Dict[String, ast.Decl] {}\n  for d in old {\n    mut before.insert(store.qname(d), d)\n  }\n  mut after := Set[String] {}\n  for d in new {\n    mut after.insert(store.qname(d))\n  }\n  mut changed := Set[String] {}\n  // (the definitions others rely on that changed, and the names their\n  // users mention them by)\n  mut wide := Set[String] {}\n  mut names := Set[String] {}\n  for d in new {\n    q := store.qname(d)\n    match get(before, q) {\n      Some(o) => if o != d {\n        mut changed.insert(q)\n        if binary.interface_hash(o) != binary.interface_hash(d) {\n          mut wide.insert(q)\n          for n in mentioned_as(o) + mentioned_as(d) {\n            mut names.insert(n)\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      None => {\n        mut changed.insert(q)\n        // (what mentions a new definition's names is checked with it: a\n        // variant of the same name, say)\n        for n in mentioned_as(d) {\n          mut names.insert(n)\n        }\n      },\n    }\n  }\n  mut removed := []\n  for d in old {\n    q := store.qname(d)\n    if !contains(after, q) {\n      mut removed.push(q)\n      mut wide.insert(q)\n      for n in mentioned_as(d) {\n        mut names.insert(n)\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  mut graph := Dict[String, List[String]] {}\n  mut strings_of := Dict[String, List[String]] {}\n  for (rel, bytes) in files {\n    match binary.read_header(bytes) {\n      Ok(h) => {\n        m := deps.module_name(\"\", rel)\n        for e in h.entries {\n          q := store.qualify(m, e.name)\n          mut graph.insert(q, e.deps)\n          if len(names) > 0 && !contains(changed, q) {\n            mut strings_of.insert(q, binary.entry_strings(bytes, e))\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      Err(_) => (),\n    }\n  }\n  for q in removed {\n    mut graph.remove(q)\n  }\n  if len(changed) > 0 {\n    fresh := store.graph_of(new, changed, global)\n    for q in to_list(changed) {\n      mut graph.insert(q, get(fresh, q) ?? [])\n    }\n  }\n  mut checked := changed\n  if len(names) > 0 {\n    for q in keys(graph) {\n      if !contains(checked, q) && contains(after, q) {\n        if (get(graph, q) ?? []).any(x -> contains(wide, x))\n          || (get(strings_of, q) ?? []).any(s -> contains(names, s)) {\n          mut checked.insert(q)\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  EditScope { changed, checked, graph }\n}","old_text":"/// `files` is the package's module files before the edit (path, bytes). A\n/// body change can't break other definitions: only a changed interface or\n/// a removed definition has its users checked. Users are found through the\n/// dependencies module headers list, and, for what headers don't list (a\n/// method called on a value, a field read), through the names in their\n/// string tables.\nfn edit_scope(\n  old: List[ast.Decl],\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  files: List[(String, List[Int])],\n  global: Bool,\n) -> EditScope {\n  mut before := Dict[String, ast.Decl] {}\n  for d in old {\n    mut before.insert(store.qname(d), d)\n  }\n  mut after := Set[String] {}\n  for d in new {\n    mut after.insert(store.qname(d))\n  }\n  mut changed := Set[String] {}\n  // (the definitions others rely on that changed, and the names their\n  // users mention them by)\n  mut wide := Set[String] {}\n  mut names := Set[String] {}\n  for d in new {\n    q := store.qname(d)\n    match get(before, q) {\n      Some(o) => if o != d {\n        mut changed.insert(q)\n        if binary.interface_hash(o) != binary.interface_hash(d) {\n          mut wide.insert(q)\n          for n in mentioned_as(o) + mentioned_as(d) {\n            mut names.insert(n)\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      None => {\n        mut changed.insert(q)\n        // (what mentions a new definition's names is checked with it: a\n        // variant of the same name, say)\n        for n in mentioned_as(d) {\n          mut names.insert(n)\n        }\n      },\n    }\n  }\n  mut removed := []\n  for d in old {\n    q := store.qname(d)\n    if !contains(after, q) {\n      mut removed.push(q)\n      mut wide.insert(q)\n      for n in mentioned_as(d) {\n        mut names.insert(n)\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  mut graph := Dict[String, List[String]] {}\n  mut strings_of := Dict[String, List[String]] {}\n  for (rel, bytes) in files {\n    match binary.read_header(bytes) {\n      Ok(h) => {\n        m := deps.module_name(\"\", rel)\n        for e in h.entries {\n          q := store.qualify(m, e.name)\n          mut graph.insert(q, e.deps)\n          if len(names) > 0 && !contains(changed, q) {\n            mut strings_of.insert(q, binary.entry_strings(bytes, e))\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      Err(_) => (),\n    }\n  }\n  for q in removed {\n    mut graph.remove(q)\n  }\n  if len(changed) > 0 {\n    fresh := store.graph_of(new, changed, global)\n    for q in to_list(changed) {\n      mut graph.insert(q, get(fresh, q) ?? [])\n    }\n  }\n  mut checked := changed\n  if len(names) > 0 {\n    for q in keys(graph) {\n      if !contains(checked, q) && contains(after, q) {\n        if (get(graph, q) ?? []).any(x -> contains(wide, x))\n          || (get(strings_of, q) ?? []).any(s -> contains(names, s)) {\n          mut checked.insert(q)\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  EditScope { changed, removed, checked, graph }\n}"}]}
{"id":"2cf5749b4a58be15","time":1795656606,"message":"fix check.tested_in","changes":[{"name":"check.tested_in","kind":"fn","old":"3bf303c4962487fc","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"check","old_text":"/// The variables an expression tests with `is` (`x is Int`).\nfn tested_in(e: ast.Expr, out: Set[String]) -> Set[String] {\n  mut acc := match e {\n    ast.IsExpr { value: ast.Var(x), .. } => {\n      mut copy := out\n      mut copy.insert(x)\n      copy\n    },\n    _ => out,\n  }\n  for c in check.children(e) {\n    acc = check.tested_in(c, acc)\n  }\n  acc\n}"}],"fixed":["check.tested_in"]}
{"id":"b7caa9b2eaaac990","time":1795656857,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"graph.Shape","kind":"type","old":"d39a596ba5a8d7c3","new":"db7bbb3113ef7bc6","interface_changed":true,"affected":["graph.call_edges","graph.trace_graph","graph_command","command_line","main","codegen.entry","codegen.generate","codegen.new_gen","codegen.compiled_alone","eval.run","codegen_with","core_rt_text","computed_value","repl_eval","codegen.read_back","eval_files","codegen_text","literal_errors","compiled_drivers","compiling","replay_all","test_command","std_library","built_ir","core_rt_object","build_core_command","comptime_value","repl_command","codegen_file","jit_file","fuzz_file","alongside_command","literal_errors_of","verify_file","graph_runs","replay","or_solver_inputs","strata_command","check_command","verify_command","build_command","run_command","static_graph","program_objects","comptime_values","call_command","loaded_errors","edit_file","file_errors","edit_errors","build_proofs","search_invariants","check_fn","graph_diff","linked","expanded","comptime_runner","package_errors","edit_command","check_files","apply_change","apply_edit","fix_loops","diff_command","with_base","rename_command","move_command","fix_command","edit_in_editor"],"module":"graph","text":"/// A function as `trace_graph` reads its calls: its label, and where the type\n/// is in its parameters and result.\ntype Shape = {\n  label: String,\n  ins: List[graph.Place],\n  outs: List[List[graph.Step]],\n}","old_text":"/// A function as `trace_graph` reads its calls: its name in the trace, its\n/// label, and where the type is in its parameters and result.\ntype Shape = {\n  traced: String,\n  label: String,\n  ins: List[graph.Place],\n  outs: List[List[graph.Step]],\n}"},{"name":"graph.trace_graph","kind":"fn","old":"152adfc4efface6c","new":"91c77c8823cdb62f","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"graph","text":"/// The graph of a run. `trace` holds the lines of `strata run --trace`\n/// (`→ f(args)`, `← f: value`). Each call of a moving function counts the\n/// moves from its arguments to its result. A `mut` parameter's new value\n/// isn't traced, so such functions are listed as left out.\npub fn trace_graph(\n  decls: List[ast.Decl],\n  s: graph.Subject,\n  trace: String,\n) -> graph.Graph {\n  types := graph.type_table(decls)\n  mut shapes := Dict[String, graph.Shape] {}\n  mut skipped := []\n  for (_, label, traced, f) in graph.functions(decls) {\n    (ins, outs) := graph.places(types, s, f)\n    if ins.any(i -> i.mutable) {\n      mut skipped.push(\n        (\n          label,\n          \"its `mut` parameters' new values are not in the trace\",\n        ),\n      )\n    }\n    if outs != [] {\n      mut shapes.insert(traced, graph.Shape { label, ins, outs })\n    }\n  }\n  mut stack := []\n  mut edges := []\n  for l in lines(trace) {\n    match graph.after_arrow(l, \"→\") {\n      Some(call) => {\n        open := index_of(call, \"(\") ?? byte_len(call)\n        name := byte_slice(call, 0, open)\n        args := match get(shapes, name) {\n          Some(_) => match parse.parse_expr(\n            \"graph_call\" + byte_slice(call, open, byte_len(call)),\n          ) {\n            Ok(ast.Call { args, .. }) => args,\n            _ => [],\n          },\n          None => [],\n        }\n        mut stack.push((name, args))\n      },\n      None => match graph.after_arrow(l, \"←\") {\n        Some(ret) => {\n          colon := index_of(ret, \": \")\n          name := match colon {\n            Some(c) => byte_slice(ret, 0, c),\n            None => ret,\n          }\n          match get(stack, len(stack) - 1) {\n            Some((n, args)) => {\n              stack = take(stack, len(stack) - 1)\n              match get(shapes, n) {\n                Some(shape) => if n == name {\n                  value := match colon {\n                    Some(c) => match parse.parse_expr(\n                      byte_slice(ret, c + 2, byte_len(ret)),\n                    ) {\n                      Ok(v) => Some(v),\n                      Err(_) => None,\n                    },\n                    None => None,\n                  }\n                  edges += graph.call_edges(shape, args, value)\n                },\n                None => (),\n              }\n            },\n            None => (),\n          }\n        },\n        None => (),\n      },\n    }\n  }\n  graph.Graph { subject: s, edges: graph.merged(edges), skipped }\n}","old_text":"/// The graph of a run. `trace` holds the lines of `strata run --trace`\n/// (`→ f(args)`, `← f: value`). Each call of a moving function counts the\n/// moves from its arguments to its result. A `mut` parameter's new value\n/// isn't traced, so such functions are listed as left out.\npub fn trace_graph(\n  decls: List[ast.Decl],\n  s: graph.Subject,\n  trace: String,\n) -> graph.Graph {\n  types := graph.type_table(decls)\n  mut shapes := Dict[String, graph.Shape] {}\n  mut skipped := []\n  for (_, label, traced, f) in graph.functions(decls) {\n    (ins, outs) := graph.places(types, s, f)\n    if ins.any(i -> i.mutable) {\n      mut skipped.push(\n        (\n          label,\n          \"its `mut` parameters' new values are not in the trace\",\n        ),\n      )\n    }\n    if outs != [] {\n      mut shapes.insert(\n        traced,\n        graph.Shape { traced, label, ins, outs },\n      )\n    }\n  }\n  mut stack := []\n  mut edges := []\n  for l in lines(trace) {\n    match graph.after_arrow(l, \"→\") {\n      Some(call) => {\n        open := index_of(call, \"(\") ?? byte_len(call)\n        name := byte_slice(call, 0, open)\n        args := match get(shapes, name) {\n          Some(_) => match parse.parse_expr(\n            \"graph_call\" + byte_slice(call, open, byte_len(call)),\n          ) {\n            Ok(ast.Call { args, .. }) => args,\n            _ => [],\n          },\n          None => [],\n        }\n        mut stack.push((name, args))\n      },\n      None => match graph.after_arrow(l, \"←\") {\n        Some(ret) => {\n          colon := index_of(ret, \": \")\n          name := match colon {\n            Some(c) => byte_slice(ret, 0, c),\n            None => ret,\n          }\n          match get(stack, len(stack) - 1) {\n            Some((n, args)) => {\n              stack = take(stack, len(stack) - 1)\n              match get(shapes, n) {\n                Some(shape) => if n == name {\n                  value := match colon {\n                    Some(c) => match parse.parse_expr(\n                      byte_slice(ret, c + 2, byte_len(ret)),\n                    ) {\n                      Ok(v) => Some(v),\n                      Err(_) => None,\n                    },\n                    None => None,\n                  }\n                  edges += graph.call_edges(shape, args, value)\n                },\n                None => (),\n              }\n            },\n            None => (),\n          }\n        },\n        None => (),\n      },\n    }\n  }\n  graph.Graph { subject: s, edges: graph.merged(edges), skipped }\n}"}]}
{"id":"4d087a388f806f93","time":1795656980,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"check.fits","kind":"fn","old":"78907bf41dcfb2f6","new":"a9b18c2990425ce1","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"check","text":"/// A value of type `got` can go where `want` is asked for: the same type\n/// (binding type variables), or variants of the sum asked for.\nfn fits(mut i: check.Inf, want: check.Ty, got: check.Ty) -> Bool {\n  match (check.res(i, want), check.res(i, got)) {\n    (check.TNamed { name: w, .. }, check.TVariants { owner, .. }) => w == owner,\n    (check.TVariants { owner: w, names: ws }, check.TVariants { owner, names }) => w == owner && names.all(n -> ws.contains(n)),\n    // a union holds its members, and the members of a smaller union\n    (check.TUnion(ws), check.TUnion(gs)) => gs.all(g -> check.member_of(ws, g)),\n    (check.TUnion(ws), g) => check.member_of(ws, g),\n    // values are never shared, so a `List[Circle]` reads as a `List[Shape]`:\n    // type arguments fit member-wise (`call` holds a `mut` parameter to the\n    // exact type)\n    (check.TList(w), check.TList(g)) => check.fits(mut i, w, g),\n    // a finite iterator where a list is wanted (a field, an annotation, a\n    // result) is the list it holds (codegen's `converted` calls `to_list`)\n    (check.TList(_), check.TNamed { .. }) => if check.implements(i, check.res(i, got), \"FiniteIterator\") {\n      match check.trait_method(\n        i,\n        \"FiniteIterator\",\n        \"to_list\",\n        check.res(i, got),\n        8,\n      ) {\n        Some(check.TFn { ret, .. }) => check.fits(mut i, want, ret),\n        _ => false,\n      }\n    } else {\n      check.unify(mut i, want, got, 100)\n    },\n    (check.TNamed { name: n, args: was }, check.TNamed { name: m, args: gas }) => if n == m && len(was) == len(gas) && len(was) > 0 {\n      mut ok := true\n      mut k := 0\n      while k < len(was) {\n        ok = ok && check.fits(mut i, was[k], gas[k])\n        k += 1\n      }\n      ok\n    } else {\n      check.unify(mut i, want, got, 100)\n    },\n    _ => check.unify(mut i, want, got, 100),\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// A value of type `got` can go where `want` is asked for: the same type\n/// (binding type variables), or variants of the sum asked for.\nfn fits(mut i: check.Inf, want: check.Ty, got: check.Ty) -> Bool {\n  match (check.res(i, want), check.res(i, got)) {\n    (check.TNamed { name: w, .. }, check.TVariants { owner, .. }) => w == owner,\n    (check.TVariants { owner: w, names: ws }, check.TVariants { owner, names }) => w == owner && names.all(n -> ws.contains(n)),\n    // a union holds its members, and the members of a smaller union\n    (check.TUnion(ws), check.TUnion(gs)) => gs.all(g -> check.member_of(ws, g)),\n    (check.TUnion(ws), g) => check.member_of(ws, g),\n    // values are never shared, so a `List[Circle]` reads as a `List[Shape]`:\n    // type arguments fit member-wise (`call` holds a `mut` parameter to the\n    // exact type)\n    (check.TList(w), check.TList(g)) => check.fits(mut i, w, g),\n    // a finite iterator where a list is wanted (a field, an annotation, a\n    // result) is the list it holds (codegen's `converted` calls `to_list`)\n    (check.TList(_), check.TNamed { name, .. }) => if check.implements(i, check.res(i, got), \"FiniteIterator\") {\n      match check.trait_method(\n        i,\n        \"FiniteIterator\",\n        \"to_list\",\n        check.res(i, got),\n        8,\n      ) {\n        Some(check.TFn { ret, .. }) => check.fits(mut i, want, ret),\n        _ => false,\n      }\n    } else {\n      check.unify(mut i, want, got, 100)\n    },\n    (check.TNamed { name: n, args: was }, check.TNamed { name: m, args: gas }) => if n == m && len(was) == len(gas) && len(was) > 0 {\n      mut ok := true\n      mut k := 0\n      while k < len(was) {\n        ok = ok && check.fits(mut i, was[k], gas[k])\n        k += 1\n      }\n      ok\n    } else {\n      check.unify(mut i, want, got, 100)\n    },\n    _ => check.unify(mut i, want, got, 100),\n  }\n}"}]}
{"id":"36b5a31e593c6264","time":1795656988,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"codegen.string_builtin","kind":"fn","old":"e1c6c0048651cb43","new":"b9d2046e1099f010","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","text":"/// String built-ins: runtime.c's, or the prelude's `str_…`.\nfn string_builtin(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  name: String,\n  vs: List[codegen.V],\n) -> codegen.V {\n  match (name, len(vs)) {\n    (\"split\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_split\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"contains\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_contains\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"starts_with\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_starts_with\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"ends_with\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_ends_with\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"reverse\", 1) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_reverse\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"chars\", 1) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_chars\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"lines\", 1) => codegen.call_fn(mut g, codegen.prelude_name(\"lines\"), vs, []),\n    (\"index_of\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_index_of\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"replace\", 3) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_replace\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"repeat\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_repeat\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"trim\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_trim\", vs),\n    (\"to_upper\", 1) | (\"to_lower\", 1) => {\n      (table, n) := codegen.unicode_table(mut g, if name == \"to_upper\" {\n        \"upper\"\n      } else {\n        \"lower\"\n      })\n      (cased, m) := codegen.unicode_table(mut g, \"cased\")\n      codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_case\", [\n        get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit(),\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: table },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: to_string(n) },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: cased },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: to_string(m) },\n        codegen.V {\n          ty: check.TBool,\n          op: to_string(name == \"to_lower\"),\n        },\n      ])\n    },\n    (\"is_digit\", 1) | (\"is_alpha\", 1) | (\"is_space\", 1) => {\n      (ranges, n) := codegen.unicode_table(mut g, \"alpha\")\n      class := match name {\n        \"is_digit\" => \"0\",\n        \"is_alpha\" => \"1\",\n        _ => \"2\",\n      }\n      codegen.call(mut g, check.TBool, \"strata_str_is\", [\n        get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit(),\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: class },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: ranges },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: to_string(n) },\n      ])\n    },\n    (\"len\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_len\", vs),\n    (\"get\", 2) => {\n      c := codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_at\", vs)\n      ok := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"found\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{ok} = icmp ne ptr {c.op}, null\")\n      codegen.option_if(mut g, ok, c, codegen.option_of(check.TStr))\n    },\n    (\"at\", 2) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_at_or_fault\", vs),\n    (\"slice\", 3) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_slice\", vs),\n    (\"ord\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_ord\", vs),\n    (\"byte_len\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_byte_len\", vs),\n    (\"byte_at\", 2) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_byte_at\", vs),\n    (\"byte_slice\", 3) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_byte_slice\", vs),\n    (\"chr\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_chr\", vs),\n    (\"parse_int\", 1) | (\"parse_float\", 1) => {\n      t := if name == \"parse_int\" {\n        check.TInt\n      } else {\n        check.TFloat\n      }\n      slot := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"parsed\")\n      mut g.allocas.push(f\"  {slot} = alloca {codegen.ll(t)}\")\n      zero := if name == \"parse_int\" {\n        \"0\"\n      } else {\n        \"0.0\"\n      }\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"store {codegen.ll(t)} {zero}, ptr {slot}\",\n      )\n      ok := codegen.call(mut g, check.TBool, \"strata_\" + name, [\n        get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit(),\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: slot },\n      ])\n      x := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"x\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{x} = load {codegen.ll(t)}, ptr {slot}\")\n      // the parsed number is new: a big one is an object, moved into the option\n      xv := codegen.temp(mut g, codegen.V { ty: t, op: x })\n      codegen.option_if(mut g, ok.op, xv, codegen.option_of(t))\n    },\n    (\"to_string\", 1) => codegen.show(mut g, get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit()),\n    (\"debug\", 1) => codegen.shown(mut g, get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit()),\n    (\"print\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TUnit, \"strata_print\", vs),\n    _ => {\n      codegen.not_yet(\n        mut g,\n        \"the built-in `\" + name + \"` on a `String`\",\n      )\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// String built-ins: runtime.c's, or the prelude's `str_…`.\nfn string_builtin(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  name: String,\n  vs: List[codegen.V],\n) -> codegen.V {\n  strings := check.TList(check.TStr)\n  match (name, len(vs)) {\n    (\"split\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_split\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"contains\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_contains\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"starts_with\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_starts_with\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"ends_with\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_ends_with\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"reverse\", 1) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_reverse\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"chars\", 1) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_chars\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"lines\", 1) => codegen.call_fn(mut g, codegen.prelude_name(\"lines\"), vs, []),\n    (\"index_of\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_index_of\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"replace\", 3) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_replace\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"repeat\", 2) => codegen.call_fn(\n      mut g,\n      codegen.prelude_name(\"str_repeat\"),\n      vs,\n      [],\n    ),\n    (\"trim\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_trim\", vs),\n    (\"to_upper\", 1) | (\"to_lower\", 1) => {\n      (table, n) := codegen.unicode_table(mut g, if name == \"to_upper\" {\n        \"upper\"\n      } else {\n        \"lower\"\n      })\n      (cased, m) := codegen.unicode_table(mut g, \"cased\")\n      codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_case\", [\n        get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit(),\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: table },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: to_string(n) },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: cased },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: to_string(m) },\n        codegen.V {\n          ty: check.TBool,\n          op: to_string(name == \"to_lower\"),\n        },\n      ])\n    },\n    (\"is_digit\", 1) | (\"is_alpha\", 1) | (\"is_space\", 1) => {\n      (ranges, n) := codegen.unicode_table(mut g, \"alpha\")\n      class := match name {\n        \"is_digit\" => \"0\",\n        \"is_alpha\" => \"1\",\n        _ => \"2\",\n      }\n      codegen.call(mut g, check.TBool, \"strata_str_is\", [\n        get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit(),\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: class },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: ranges },\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: to_string(n) },\n      ])\n    },\n    (\"len\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_len\", vs),\n    (\"get\", 2) => {\n      c := codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_at\", vs)\n      ok := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"found\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{ok} = icmp ne ptr {c.op}, null\")\n      codegen.option_if(mut g, ok, c, codegen.option_of(check.TStr))\n    },\n    (\"at\", 2) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_at_or_fault\", vs),\n    (\"slice\", 3) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_slice\", vs),\n    (\"ord\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_ord\", vs),\n    (\"byte_len\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_byte_len\", vs),\n    (\"byte_at\", 2) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_str_byte_at\", vs),\n    (\"byte_slice\", 3) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_byte_slice\", vs),\n    (\"chr\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_str_chr\", vs),\n    (\"parse_int\", 1) | (\"parse_float\", 1) => {\n      t := if name == \"parse_int\" {\n        check.TInt\n      } else {\n        check.TFloat\n      }\n      slot := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"parsed\")\n      mut g.allocas.push(f\"  {slot} = alloca {codegen.ll(t)}\")\n      zero := if name == \"parse_int\" {\n        \"0\"\n      } else {\n        \"0.0\"\n      }\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"store {codegen.ll(t)} {zero}, ptr {slot}\",\n      )\n      ok := codegen.call(mut g, check.TBool, \"strata_\" + name, [\n        get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit(),\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: slot },\n      ])\n      x := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"x\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{x} = load {codegen.ll(t)}, ptr {slot}\")\n      // the parsed number is new: a big one is an object, moved into the option\n      xv := codegen.temp(mut g, codegen.V { ty: t, op: x })\n      codegen.option_if(mut g, ok.op, xv, codegen.option_of(t))\n    },\n    (\"to_string\", 1) => codegen.show(mut g, get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit()),\n    (\"debug\", 1) => codegen.shown(mut g, get(vs, 0) ?? codegen.unit()),\n    (\"print\", 1) => codegen.call(mut g, check.TUnit, \"strata_print\", vs),\n    _ => {\n      codegen.not_yet(\n        mut g,\n        \"the built-in `\" + name + \"` on a `String`\",\n      )\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n  }\n}"},{"name":"codegen.union_cmp","kind":"fn","old":"4f6c41c497708bc8","new":"2eaece3427ed6b25","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","text":"/// The order of union values: by member index, then as that member.\nfn union_cmp(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  a: codegen.V,\n  b: codegen.V,\n  ms: List[check.Ty],\n) {\n  la := codegen.on_members(mut g, a, ms)\n  for (i, ma) in enumerate(ms) {\n    codegen.block(mut g, get(la, i) ?? \"\")\n    lb := codegen.on_members(mut g, b, ms)\n    for (j, _) in enumerate(ms) {\n      codegen.block(mut g, get(lb, j) ?? \"\")\n      if i != j {\n        codegen.emit(mut g, if i < j {\n          \"ret i64 -1\"\n        } else {\n          \"ret i64 1\"\n        })\n      } else {\n        f := codegen.cmp_helper(mut g, ma)\n        x := codegen.narrow(mut g, a, ma)\n        y := codegen.narrow(mut g, b, ma)\n        c := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"c\")\n        args := join([x, y]\n          .filter(v -> codegen.has_value(v.ty))\n          .map(v -> codegen.ll(v.ty) + \" \" + v.op), \", \")\n        codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{c} = call i64 {f}({args})\")\n        codegen.emit(mut g, f\"ret i64 {c}\")\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// The order of union values: by member index, then as that member.\nfn union_cmp(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  a: codegen.V,\n  b: codegen.V,\n  ms: List[check.Ty],\n) {\n  la := codegen.on_members(mut g, a, ms)\n  for (i, ma) in enumerate(ms) {\n    codegen.block(mut g, get(la, i) ?? \"\")\n    lb := codegen.on_members(mut g, b, ms)\n    for (j, mb) in enumerate(ms) {\n      codegen.block(mut g, get(lb, j) ?? \"\")\n      if i != j {\n        codegen.emit(mut g, if i < j {\n          \"ret i64 -1\"\n        } else {\n          \"ret i64 1\"\n        })\n      } else {\n        f := codegen.cmp_helper(mut g, ma)\n        x := codegen.narrow(mut g, a, ma)\n        y := codegen.narrow(mut g, b, ma)\n        c := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"c\")\n        args := join([x, y]\n          .filter(v -> codegen.has_value(v.ty))\n          .map(v -> codegen.ll(v.ty) + \" \" + v.op), \", \")\n        codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{c} = call i64 {f}({args})\")\n        codegen.emit(mut g, f\"ret i64 {c}\")\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"name":"codegen.produce","kind":"fn","old":"b031e0ab2bc783a7","new":"75c6b1226a59fe5a","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","text":"/// A generator's body: an owned value of `t` (of type `ty`) at `%depth`.\nfn produce(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  t: ast.TypeExpr,\n  ty: check.Ty,\n  h: codegen.Hints,\n) -> codegen.V {\n  match t {\n    ast.UnitType => return codegen.unit(),\n    // a union: a member picked at run time\n    ast.UnionType(ms) => {\n      codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_random\")\n      which := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"which\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{which} = call i64 @strata_random(i64 0, i64 {len(ms) - 1})\",\n      )\n      slot := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"u\")\n      mut g.allocas.push(f\"  {slot} = alloca {codegen.ll(ty)}\")\n      end := codegen.label(mut g, \"u.end\")\n      mut labels := []\n      for _ in ms {\n        mut labels.push(codegen.label(mut g, \"u.member\"))\n      }\n      mut cases := []\n      for (k, l) in enumerate(labels) {\n        mut cases.push(f\"i64 {k}, label %{l}\")\n      }\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"switch i64 {which}, label %{get(labels, 0) ?? end} [ {join(cases, \" \")} ]\",\n      )\n      for (k, m) in enumerate(ms) {\n        codegen.block(mut g, get(labels, k) ?? end)\n        codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n        v := codegen.generated(mut g, m, codegen.no_hints(), \"%depth\")\n        x := codegen.temp(mut g, v)\n        u := codegen.converted(mut g, x, ty)\n        held := codegen.take_value(mut g, u)\n        codegen.pop_scope(mut g)\n        codegen.emit(\n          mut g,\n          f\"store {codegen.ll(ty)} {held.op}, ptr {slot}\",\n        )\n        codegen.br(mut g, end)\n      }\n      codegen.block(mut g, end)\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"uv\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{r} = load {codegen.ll(ty)}, ptr {slot}\",\n      )\n      return codegen.V { ty, op: r }\n    },\n    // a function: returns a value generated on the first call per\n    // arguments, since a function always gives the same result for the same\n    // arguments\n    ast.FnType { params, ret } => {\n      codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n      d := codegen.deeper(mut g)\n      r := codegen.generated(mut g, ret, codegen.no_hints(), d)\n      codegen.local_owned(mut g, \"gen.result\", r)\n      mut ps := []\n      for (k, p) in enumerate(params) {\n        mut ps.push(ast.LamParam { name: f\"gen.p{k}\", ty: Some(p) })\n      }\n      f := codegen.lambda(mut g, ps, ast.Var(\"gen.result\"), ty)\n      x := codegen.take_value(mut g, f)\n      codegen.pop_scope(mut g)\n      return x\n    },\n    ast.Refined { base, pred } => {\n      h2 := codegen.hints_and(h, pred)\n      (head, fail) := codegen.tries_start(mut g, 300)\n      v := codegen.generated(mut g, base, h2, \"%depth\")\n      x := codegen.V { ty, op: v.op }\n      ok := codegen.satisfies(mut g, t, x)\n      codegen.tries_end(\n        mut g,\n        x,\n        ok,\n        head,\n        fail,\n        f\"could not generate a value satisfying `{text.type_text(t)}` after 300 attempts\",\n      )\n      return x\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  (n, args) := match t {\n    ast.Named { name, args } => (name, args),\n    _ => {\n      codegen.not_yet(\n        mut g,\n        \"generating a value of `\" + text.type_text(t) + \"`\",\n      )\n      return codegen.never()\n    },\n  }\n  match codegen.sized(ty) {\n    Some(_) => {\n      (tbl, k) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, codegen.bounded(h.ints, 1000, 100))\n      codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_int\")\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"i\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{r} = call i64 @strata_gen_int(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k})\",\n      )\n      return codegen.as_type(\n        mut g,\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: r },\n        ty,\n      )\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  if n == \"Int\" || n == \"Float\" {\n    (tbl, k) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, codegen.bounded(h.ints, 1000, 100))\n    r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"i\")\n    if n == \"Int\" {\n      codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_int\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{r} = call i64 @strata_gen_int(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k})\",\n      )\n      return codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: r }\n    }\n    (rt, rk) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, h.ints)\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_float\")\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{r} = call double @strata_gen_float(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k}, ptr {rt}, i64 {rk})\",\n    )\n    return codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: r }\n  }\n  if n == \"Bool\" {\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_random\")\n    (x, r) := (codegen.fresh(mut g, \"b\"), codegen.fresh(mut g, \"b\"))\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{x} = call i64 @strata_random(i64 0, i64 1)\",\n    )\n    codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = trunc i64 {x} to i1\")\n    return codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: r }\n  }\n  if n == \"String\" {\n    match h.regex {\n      // strings matching the refinement's regex, made at compile time (the\n      // same every run), one picked at run time\n      Some(re) => match std.regex.samples(re, 32, 7) {\n        Ok(xs) => if xs != [] {\n          mut consts := []\n          for x in xs {\n            mut consts.push(\"ptr \" + codegen.string(mut g, x))\n          }\n          g.lambdas += 1\n          name := f\"@\\\"samples.{g.owner}{g.lambdas}\\\"\"\n          codegen.add_helper(mut g, name)\n          mut g.globals.push(\n            f\"{name} = private unnamed_addr constant [{len(consts)} x ptr] [{join(consts, \", \")}], align 8\",\n          )\n          codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_random\")\n          (i, at, r) := (\n            codegen.fresh(mut g, \"which\"),\n            codegen.fresh(mut g, \"at\"),\n            codegen.fresh(mut g, \"s\"),\n          )\n          codegen.emit(\n            mut g,\n            f\"{i} = call i64 @strata_random(i64 0, i64 {len(consts) - 1})\",\n          )\n          codegen.emit(\n            mut g,\n            f\"{at} = getelementptr ptr, ptr {name}, i64 {i}\",\n          )\n          codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = load ptr, ptr {at}\")\n          return codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: r }\n        } else {\n          codegen.not_yet(\n            mut g,\n            f\"strings matching {debug(re)}: it has no samples\",\n          )\n          return codegen.never()\n        },\n        Err(m) => {\n          codegen.not_yet(\n            mut g,\n            f\"strings matching {debug(re)}: {m}\",\n          )\n          return codegen.never()\n        },\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n    (tbl, k) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, codegen.bounded(h.lens, 0, 8))\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_len\")\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_string\")\n    (l, r) := (codegen.fresh(mut g, \"len\"), codegen.fresh(mut g, \"s\"))\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{l} = call i64 @strata_gen_len(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k})\",\n    )\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{r} = call ptr @strata_gen_string(i64 {l})\",\n    )\n    return codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: r }\n  }\n  if n == \"Tuple\" {\n    codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n    d := codegen.deeper(mut g)\n    mut vs := []\n    for a in args {\n      v := codegen.generated(mut g, a, codegen.no_hints(), d)\n      mut vs.push(codegen.temp(mut g, v))\n    }\n    b := codegen.block_of(mut g, 0, vs)\n    codegen.pop_scope(mut g)\n    return codegen.V { ty, op: b }\n  }\n  if n == \"List\" || n == \"Set\" || n == \"Dict\" {\n    return codegen.gen_list(mut g, n, args, ty, h)\n  }\n  match ty {\n    check.TTrait(_) => {\n      v := codegen.mock_value(mut g, ty)\n      return codegen.take_value(mut g, v)\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  // A refined alias (`type Score = Int where …`): its base within the\n  // predicate's intervals, until it holds. A plain alias: its body. A\n  // `distinct` type is a block holding its value, made by `gen_data`.\n  match get(g.refines, n) {\n    Some((base0, pred)) => {\n      itself := ast.Named { name: n, args: [] }\n      // a generic one's arguments substituted: `NonEmpty[Line]` is a\n      // `List[Line]`\n      ps := get(g.refine_params, n) ?? []\n      base := if ps != [] && len(ps) == len(args) {\n        codegen.written_in(base0, ps, args)\n      } else {\n        base0\n      }\n      if base != itself && !contains(g.distincts, n) {\n        (head, fail) := codegen.tries_start(mut g, 300)\n        v := codegen.generated(\n          mut g,\n          base,\n          codegen.hints_and(codegen.no_hints(), pred),\n          \"%depth\",\n        )\n        x := codegen.V { ty, op: v.op }\n        ok := codegen.satisfies(mut g, t, x)\n        codegen.tries_end(\n          mut g,\n          x,\n          ok,\n          head,\n          fail,\n          f\"could not generate a value satisfying `{text.type_text(t)}` after 300 attempts\",\n        )\n        return x\n      }\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  match get(g.types.aliases, n) {\n    Some(a) => {\n      v := codegen.generated(mut g, a, h, \"%depth\")\n      return codegen.V { ty, op: v.op }\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  codegen.gen_data(mut g, t, n, args, ty)\n}","old_text":"/// A generator's body: an owned value of `t` (of type `ty`) at `%depth`.\nfn produce(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  t: ast.TypeExpr,\n  ty: check.Ty,\n  h: codegen.Hints,\n) -> codegen.V {\n  match t {\n    ast.UnitType => return codegen.unit(),\n    // a union: a member picked at run time\n    ast.UnionType(ms) => {\n      codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_random\")\n      which := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"which\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{which} = call i64 @strata_random(i64 0, i64 {len(ms) - 1})\",\n      )\n      slot := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"u\")\n      mut g.allocas.push(f\"  {slot} = alloca {codegen.ll(ty)}\")\n      end := codegen.label(mut g, \"u.end\")\n      mut labels := []\n      for _ in ms {\n        mut labels.push(codegen.label(mut g, \"u.member\"))\n      }\n      mut cases := []\n      for (k, l) in enumerate(labels) {\n        mut cases.push(f\"i64 {k}, label %{l}\")\n      }\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"switch i64 {which}, label %{get(labels, 0) ?? end} [ {join(cases, \" \")} ]\",\n      )\n      for (k, m) in enumerate(ms) {\n        codegen.block(mut g, get(labels, k) ?? end)\n        codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n        v := codegen.generated(mut g, m, codegen.no_hints(), \"%depth\")\n        x := codegen.temp(mut g, v)\n        u := codegen.converted(mut g, x, ty)\n        held := codegen.take_value(mut g, u)\n        codegen.pop_scope(mut g)\n        codegen.emit(\n          mut g,\n          f\"store {codegen.ll(ty)} {held.op}, ptr {slot}\",\n        )\n        codegen.br(mut g, end)\n      }\n      codegen.block(mut g, end)\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"uv\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{r} = load {codegen.ll(ty)}, ptr {slot}\",\n      )\n      return codegen.V { ty, op: r }\n    },\n    // a function: returns a value generated on the first call per\n    // arguments, since a function always gives the same result for the same\n    // arguments\n    ast.FnType { params, ret } => {\n      codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n      d := codegen.deeper(mut g)\n      r := codegen.generated(mut g, ret, codegen.no_hints(), d)\n      codegen.local_owned(mut g, \"gen.result\", r)\n      mut ps := []\n      for (k, p) in enumerate(params) {\n        mut ps.push(ast.LamParam { name: f\"gen.p{k}\", ty: Some(p) })\n      }\n      f := codegen.lambda(mut g, ps, ast.Var(\"gen.result\"), ty)\n      x := codegen.take_value(mut g, f)\n      codegen.pop_scope(mut g)\n      return x\n    },\n    ast.Refined { base, pred } => {\n      h2 := codegen.hints_and(h, pred)\n      (head, fail) := codegen.tries_start(mut g, 300)\n      v := codegen.generated(mut g, base, h2, \"%depth\")\n      x := codegen.V { ty, op: v.op }\n      ok := codegen.satisfies(mut g, t, x)\n      codegen.tries_end(\n        mut g,\n        x,\n        ok,\n        head,\n        fail,\n        f\"could not generate a value satisfying `{text.type_text(t)}` after 300 attempts\",\n      )\n      return x\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  (n, args) := match t {\n    ast.Named { name, args } => (name, args),\n    _ => {\n      codegen.not_yet(\n        mut g,\n        \"generating a value of `\" + text.type_text(t) + \"`\",\n      )\n      return codegen.never()\n    },\n  }\n  match codegen.sized(ty) {\n    Some(w) => {\n      (tbl, k) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, codegen.bounded(h.ints, 1000, 100))\n      codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_int\")\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"i\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{r} = call i64 @strata_gen_int(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k})\",\n      )\n      return codegen.as_type(\n        mut g,\n        codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: r },\n        ty,\n      )\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  if n == \"Int\" || n == \"Float\" {\n    (tbl, k) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, codegen.bounded(h.ints, 1000, 100))\n    r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"i\")\n    if n == \"Int\" {\n      codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_int\")\n      codegen.emit(\n        mut g,\n        f\"{r} = call i64 @strata_gen_int(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k})\",\n      )\n      return codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: r }\n    }\n    (rt, rk) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, h.ints)\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_float\")\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{r} = call double @strata_gen_float(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k}, ptr {rt}, i64 {rk})\",\n    )\n    return codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: r }\n  }\n  if n == \"Bool\" {\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_random\")\n    (x, r) := (codegen.fresh(mut g, \"b\"), codegen.fresh(mut g, \"b\"))\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{x} = call i64 @strata_random(i64 0, i64 1)\",\n    )\n    codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = trunc i64 {x} to i1\")\n    return codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: r }\n  }\n  if n == \"String\" {\n    match h.regex {\n      // strings matching the refinement's regex, made at compile time (the\n      // same every run), one picked at run time\n      Some(re) => match std.regex.samples(re, 32, 7) {\n        Ok(xs) => if xs != [] {\n          mut consts := []\n          for x in xs {\n            mut consts.push(\"ptr \" + codegen.string(mut g, x))\n          }\n          g.lambdas += 1\n          name := f\"@\\\"samples.{g.owner}{g.lambdas}\\\"\"\n          codegen.add_helper(mut g, name)\n          mut g.globals.push(\n            f\"{name} = private unnamed_addr constant [{len(consts)} x ptr] [{join(consts, \", \")}], align 8\",\n          )\n          codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_random\")\n          (i, at, r) := (\n            codegen.fresh(mut g, \"which\"),\n            codegen.fresh(mut g, \"at\"),\n            codegen.fresh(mut g, \"s\"),\n          )\n          codegen.emit(\n            mut g,\n            f\"{i} = call i64 @strata_random(i64 0, i64 {len(consts) - 1})\",\n          )\n          codegen.emit(\n            mut g,\n            f\"{at} = getelementptr ptr, ptr {name}, i64 {i}\",\n          )\n          codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = load ptr, ptr {at}\")\n          return codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: r }\n        } else {\n          codegen.not_yet(\n            mut g,\n            f\"strings matching {debug(re)}: it has no samples\",\n          )\n          return codegen.never()\n        },\n        Err(m) => {\n          codegen.not_yet(\n            mut g,\n            f\"strings matching {debug(re)}: {m}\",\n          )\n          return codegen.never()\n        },\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n    (tbl, k) := codegen.pairs_table(mut g, codegen.bounded(h.lens, 0, 8))\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_len\")\n    codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_gen_string\")\n    (l, r) := (codegen.fresh(mut g, \"len\"), codegen.fresh(mut g, \"s\"))\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{l} = call i64 @strata_gen_len(ptr {tbl}, i64 {k})\",\n    )\n    codegen.emit(\n      mut g,\n      f\"{r} = call ptr @strata_gen_string(i64 {l})\",\n    )\n    return codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: r }\n  }\n  if n == \"Tuple\" {\n    codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n    d := codegen.deeper(mut g)\n    mut vs := []\n    for a in args {\n      v := codegen.generated(mut g, a, codegen.no_hints(), d)\n      mut vs.push(codegen.temp(mut g, v))\n    }\n    b := codegen.block_of(mut g, 0, vs)\n    codegen.pop_scope(mut g)\n    return codegen.V { ty, op: b }\n  }\n  if n == \"List\" || n == \"Set\" || n == \"Dict\" {\n    return codegen.gen_list(mut g, n, args, ty, h)\n  }\n  match ty {\n    check.TTrait(_) => {\n      v := codegen.mock_value(mut g, ty)\n      return codegen.take_value(mut g, v)\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  // A refined alias (`type Score = Int where …`): its base within the\n  // predicate's intervals, until it holds. A plain alias: its body. A\n  // `distinct` type is a block holding its value, made by `gen_data`.\n  match get(g.refines, n) {\n    Some((base0, pred)) => {\n      itself := ast.Named { name: n, args: [] }\n      // a generic one's arguments substituted: `NonEmpty[Line]` is a\n      // `List[Line]`\n      ps := get(g.refine_params, n) ?? []\n      base := if ps != [] && len(ps) == len(args) {\n        codegen.written_in(base0, ps, args)\n      } else {\n        base0\n      }\n      if base != itself && !contains(g.distincts, n) {\n        (head, fail) := codegen.tries_start(mut g, 300)\n        v := codegen.generated(\n          mut g,\n          base,\n          codegen.hints_and(codegen.no_hints(), pred),\n          \"%depth\",\n        )\n        x := codegen.V { ty, op: v.op }\n        ok := codegen.satisfies(mut g, t, x)\n        codegen.tries_end(\n          mut g,\n          x,\n          ok,\n          head,\n          fail,\n          f\"could not generate a value satisfying `{text.type_text(t)}` after 300 attempts\",\n        )\n        return x\n      }\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  match get(g.types.aliases, n) {\n    Some(a) => {\n      v := codegen.generated(mut g, a, h, \"%depth\")\n      return codegen.V { ty, op: v.op }\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  codegen.gen_data(mut g, t, n, args, ty)\n}"},{"name":"codegen.expr_node","kind":"fn","old":"53b873c398f03f4f","new":"84fa0a9fc7d82c4a","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","text":"fn expr_node(mut g: codegen.Gen, e: ast.Expr) -> codegen.V {\n  match e {\n    ast.IntLit(n) => codegen.int_lit(mut g, n),\n    ast.BigIntLit(digits) => {\n      s := codegen.string(mut g, digits)\n      codegen.call(\n        mut g,\n        check.TInt,\n        \"strata_int_lit\",\n        [codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: s }],\n      )\n    },\n    ast.FloatLit(f) => codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: codegen.float_op(f) },\n    ast.BoolLit(b) => codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: if b {\n      \"true\"\n    } else {\n      \"false\"\n    } },\n    ast.StrLit(s) => codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: codegen.string(mut g, s) },\n    ast.UnitExpr => codegen.unit(),\n    ast.Var(x) => match codegen.lookup(g, x) {\n      Some(l) => codegen.load(mut g, l),\n      None => codegen.expr_want(mut g, e, check.TAny),\n    },\n    ast.Binary { op, left, right } => codegen.binary(mut g, op, left, right),\n    ast.Unary { op: ast.Not, operand } => {\n      v := codegen.expr(mut g, operand)\n      if v.ty is check.TAny {\n        return v\n      }\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"not\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = xor i1 {v.op}, true\")\n      codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: r }\n    },\n    ast.Unary { op: ast.Neg, operand } => {\n      v := codegen.expr(mut g, operand)\n      match codegen.sized(v.ty) {\n        Some(_) => {\n          r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"neg\")\n          codegen.emit(\n            mut g,\n            f\"{r} = sub {codegen.ll(v.ty)} 0, {v.op}\",\n          )\n          return codegen.V { ty: v.ty, op: r }\n        },\n        None => (),\n      }\n      match v.ty {\n        check.TInt => codegen.int_op(\n          mut g,\n          \"ssub\",\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: \"0\" },\n          v,\n        ),\n        check.TFloat => {\n          r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"neg\")\n          codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = fneg double {v.op}\")\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: r }\n        },\n        _ => v,\n      }\n    },\n    ast.IfExpr { cond, then, otherwise } => codegen.if_expr(mut g, cond, then, otherwise),\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => codegen.block_expr(mut g, stmts, last, check.TAny),\n    ast.Lambda { params, body } => codegen.lambda(mut g, params, body, check.TAny),\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(name), args } => if contains(g.tags, name)\n      && !(codegen.lookup(g, name) is Some)\n      && !codegen.has_fn(g, name) {\n      codegen.construct(mut g, name, ast.PositionalArgs(args))\n    } else {\n      codegen.call_named(mut g, name, args, check.TAny)\n    },\n    ast.CtorExpr { name, args } => codegen.construct(mut g, name, args),\n    ast.TupleExpr(es) => match codegen.operands(mut g, es) {\n      Some(vs) => {\n        p := codegen.block_of(mut g, 0, vs)\n        codegen.temp(mut g, codegen.V {\n          ty: check.TNamed { name: \"Tuple\", args: vs.map(v -> v.ty) },\n          op: p,\n        })\n      },\n      None => codegen.never(),\n    },\n    ast.FieldOf { base, name } => codegen.get_field(mut g, base, name),\n    ast.IsExpr { value, variant } => {\n      v := codegen.expr(mut g, value)\n      if v.ty is check.TAny {\n        return v\n      }\n      match v.ty {\n        check.TUnion(ms) => match codegen.member_named(g, ms, variant) {\n          Some(m) => if contains(g.types.ctors, variant)\n            && !(codegen.head_of(m) == variant) {\n            codegen.tag_is(mut g, codegen.V { ..v, ty: m }, variant)\n          } else {\n            codegen.holds_member(mut g, v, m)\n          },\n          None => codegen.tag_is(mut g, v, variant),\n        },\n        _ => codegen.tag_is(mut g, v, variant),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.MatchExpr { scrutinee, binding, arms } => codegen.matching(mut g, scrutinee, binding, arms),\n    // a `mut` argument or receiver mark: the call writes back\n    ast.MutExpr(x) => codegen.expr(mut g, x),\n    // an unfilled hole `?name`, which compile-time code may leave in a\n    // branch never taken: a fault if reached\n    ast.Hole(h) => {\n      codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n      m := codegen.lit(mut g, f\"reached unfilled hole `?{h}`\")\n      codegen.fault(mut g, 5, [m])\n      codegen.discard_scope(mut g)\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n    ast.Scope(b) => codegen.scope_expr(mut g, b, check.TAny),\n    ast.Spawn(b) => codegen.spawn_expr(mut g, b, false),\n    ast.SupervisedSpawn(b) => codegen.spawn_expr(mut g, b, true),\n    ast.Await(h) => codegen.await_expr(mut g, h),\n    // `old e` where nothing was taken on entry (a mock's `ensures`): `e`\n    // as is\n    ast.Old(x) => codegen.expr(mut g, x),\n    // a spread the checker did not expand: compile-time code, folded before\n    // it runs\n    ast.Spread(_) => {\n      codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n      m := codegen.lit(\n        mut g,\n        \"reached a spread (`...x`) not written out as a call\",\n      )\n      codegen.fault(mut g, 5, [m])\n      codegen.discard_scope(mut g)\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n    ast.Assumed(x) => codegen.expr(mut g, x),\n    ast.MockExpr(t) => {\n      mt := codegen.lower(mut g, t)\n      codegen.mock_value(mut g, mt)\n    },\n    ast.Select(arms) => codegen.select_expr(mut g, arms),\n    ast.Race(arms) => codegen.race_expr(mut g, arms),\n    ast.Try { value, kind } => codegen.try_expr(mut g, value, kind),\n    ast.Except { value, err, fallback } => codegen.except_expr(mut g, value, err, fallback),\n    ast.Fallback { value, fallback } => codegen.except_expr(mut g, value, None, fallback),\n    ast.ListExpr(es) => codegen.list_literal(mut g, es),\n    ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => codegen.method_call(mut g, recv, name, args, check.TAny),\n    ast.Call { callee, args } => {\n      f := codegen.expr(mut g, callee)\n      if f.ty is check.TAny {\n        return f\n      }\n      match codegen.operands(mut g, args) {\n        Some(vs) => codegen.call_closure(mut g, f, vs),\n        None => codegen.never(),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.Return(x) => {\n      v := codegen.expr_want(mut g, x, g.ret)\n      if v.ty is check.TAny {\n        return v\n      }\n      x := codegen.as_type(mut g, v, g.ret)\n      codegen.leave_with(mut g, x)\n      codegen.give_result(\n        mut g,\n        codegen.V { ..x, ty: codegen.better(g.ret, x.ty) },\n      )\n      codegen.br(mut g, \"exit\")\n      codegen.dead(mut g)\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n    ast.Interp(parts) => codegen.interp(mut g, parts),\n    other => {\n      codegen.not_yet(mut g, \"`\" + text.expr_text(other, 0) + \"`\")\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n  }\n}","old_text":"fn expr_node(mut g: codegen.Gen, e: ast.Expr) -> codegen.V {\n  match e {\n    ast.IntLit(n) => codegen.int_lit(mut g, n),\n    ast.BigIntLit(digits) => {\n      s := codegen.string(mut g, digits)\n      codegen.call(\n        mut g,\n        check.TInt,\n        \"strata_int_lit\",\n        [codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: s }],\n      )\n    },\n    ast.FloatLit(f) => codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: codegen.float_op(f) },\n    ast.BoolLit(b) => codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: if b {\n      \"true\"\n    } else {\n      \"false\"\n    } },\n    ast.StrLit(s) => codegen.V { ty: check.TStr, op: codegen.string(mut g, s) },\n    ast.UnitExpr => codegen.unit(),\n    ast.Var(x) => match codegen.lookup(g, x) {\n      Some(l) => codegen.load(mut g, l),\n      None => codegen.expr_want(mut g, e, check.TAny),\n    },\n    ast.Binary { op, left, right } => codegen.binary(mut g, op, left, right),\n    ast.Unary { op: ast.Not, operand } => {\n      v := codegen.expr(mut g, operand)\n      if v.ty is check.TAny {\n        return v\n      }\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"not\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = xor i1 {v.op}, true\")\n      codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: r }\n    },\n    ast.Unary { op: ast.Neg, operand } => {\n      v := codegen.expr(mut g, operand)\n      match codegen.sized(v.ty) {\n        Some(w) => {\n          r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"neg\")\n          codegen.emit(\n            mut g,\n            f\"{r} = sub {codegen.ll(v.ty)} 0, {v.op}\",\n          )\n          return codegen.V { ty: v.ty, op: r }\n        },\n        None => (),\n      }\n      match v.ty {\n        check.TInt => codegen.int_op(\n          mut g,\n          \"ssub\",\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: \"0\" },\n          v,\n        ),\n        check.TFloat => {\n          r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"neg\")\n          codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = fneg double {v.op}\")\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: r }\n        },\n        _ => v,\n      }\n    },\n    ast.IfExpr { cond, then, otherwise } => codegen.if_expr(mut g, cond, then, otherwise),\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => codegen.block_expr(mut g, stmts, last, check.TAny),\n    ast.Lambda { params, body } => codegen.lambda(mut g, params, body, check.TAny),\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(name), args } => if contains(g.tags, name)\n      && !(codegen.lookup(g, name) is Some)\n      && !codegen.has_fn(g, name) {\n      codegen.construct(mut g, name, ast.PositionalArgs(args))\n    } else {\n      codegen.call_named(mut g, name, args, check.TAny)\n    },\n    ast.CtorExpr { name, args } => codegen.construct(mut g, name, args),\n    ast.TupleExpr(es) => match codegen.operands(mut g, es) {\n      Some(vs) => {\n        p := codegen.block_of(mut g, 0, vs)\n        codegen.temp(mut g, codegen.V {\n          ty: check.TNamed { name: \"Tuple\", args: vs.map(v -> v.ty) },\n          op: p,\n        })\n      },\n      None => codegen.never(),\n    },\n    ast.FieldOf { base, name } => codegen.get_field(mut g, base, name),\n    ast.IsExpr { value, variant } => {\n      v := codegen.expr(mut g, value)\n      if v.ty is check.TAny {\n        return v\n      }\n      match v.ty {\n        check.TUnion(ms) => match codegen.member_named(g, ms, variant) {\n          Some(m) => if contains(g.types.ctors, variant)\n            && !(codegen.head_of(m) == variant) {\n            codegen.tag_is(mut g, codegen.V { ..v, ty: m }, variant)\n          } else {\n            codegen.holds_member(mut g, v, m)\n          },\n          None => codegen.tag_is(mut g, v, variant),\n        },\n        _ => codegen.tag_is(mut g, v, variant),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.MatchExpr { scrutinee, binding, arms } => codegen.matching(mut g, scrutinee, binding, arms),\n    // a `mut` argument or receiver mark: the call writes back\n    ast.MutExpr(x) => codegen.expr(mut g, x),\n    // an unfilled hole `?name`, which compile-time code may leave in a\n    // branch never taken: a fault if reached\n    ast.Hole(h) => {\n      codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n      m := codegen.lit(mut g, f\"reached unfilled hole `?{h}`\")\n      codegen.fault(mut g, 5, [m])\n      codegen.discard_scope(mut g)\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n    ast.Scope(b) => codegen.scope_expr(mut g, b, check.TAny),\n    ast.Spawn(b) => codegen.spawn_expr(mut g, b, false),\n    ast.SupervisedSpawn(b) => codegen.spawn_expr(mut g, b, true),\n    ast.Await(h) => codegen.await_expr(mut g, h),\n    // `old e` where nothing was taken on entry (a mock's `ensures`): `e`\n    // as is\n    ast.Old(x) => codegen.expr(mut g, x),\n    // a spread the checker did not expand: compile-time code, folded before\n    // it runs\n    ast.Spread(_) => {\n      codegen.push_scope(mut g)\n      m := codegen.lit(\n        mut g,\n        \"reached a spread (`...x`) not written out as a call\",\n      )\n      codegen.fault(mut g, 5, [m])\n      codegen.discard_scope(mut g)\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n    ast.Assumed(x) => codegen.expr(mut g, x),\n    ast.MockExpr(t) => {\n      mt := codegen.lower(mut g, t)\n      codegen.mock_value(mut g, mt)\n    },\n    ast.Select(arms) => codegen.select_expr(mut g, arms),\n    ast.Race(arms) => codegen.race_expr(mut g, arms),\n    ast.Try { value, kind } => codegen.try_expr(mut g, value, kind),\n    ast.Except { value, err, fallback } => codegen.except_expr(mut g, value, err, fallback),\n    ast.Fallback { value, fallback } => codegen.except_expr(mut g, value, None, fallback),\n    ast.ListExpr(es) => codegen.list_literal(mut g, es),\n    ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => codegen.method_call(mut g, recv, name, args, check.TAny),\n    ast.Call { callee, args } => {\n      f := codegen.expr(mut g, callee)\n      if f.ty is check.TAny {\n        return f\n      }\n      match codegen.operands(mut g, args) {\n        Some(vs) => codegen.call_closure(mut g, f, vs),\n        None => codegen.never(),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.Return(x) => {\n      v := codegen.expr_want(mut g, x, g.ret)\n      if v.ty is check.TAny {\n        return v\n      }\n      x := codegen.as_type(mut g, v, g.ret)\n      codegen.leave_with(mut g, x)\n      codegen.give_result(\n        mut g,\n        codegen.V { ..x, ty: codegen.better(g.ret, x.ty) },\n      )\n      codegen.br(mut g, \"exit\")\n      codegen.dead(mut g)\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n    ast.Interp(parts) => codegen.interp(mut g, parts),\n    other => {\n      codegen.not_yet(mut g, \"`\" + text.expr_text(other, 0) + \"`\")\n      codegen.never()\n    },\n  }\n}"}]}
{"id":"1f114a592f22c57e","time":1795657013,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"derive.expand","kind":"fn","old":"c2d420c4bdfa6526","new":"4ab517e20c738412","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"derive","text":"/// The program with each `derive` replaced by its `impl` (or an error\n/// saying why it can't be made) and each `comptime e` by its value.\npub fn expand(decls: List[ast.Decl]) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)]) {\n  derive.expand_with(\n    decls,\n    (_, _, es) -> es.map(_ -> Err(derive.not_compiled())),\n  )\n}","old_text":"/// The program with each `derive` replaced by its `impl` (or an error\n/// saying why it can't be made) and each `comptime e` by its value.\npub fn expand(decls: List[ast.Decl]) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)]) {\n  derive.expand_with(\n    decls,\n    (ds, m, es) -> es.map(e -> Err(derive.not_compiled())),\n  )\n}"},{"name":"derive.expand_in","kind":"fn","old":"458b50d7e92d0506","new":"d3e3ee0737681299","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"derive","text":"/// `expand` of definitions added to a program, with `comptime e` run by\n/// `eval`. `context` (not returned) is what their `derive`s and\n/// `comptime e` read. Expands a program's own definitions without std's.\npub fn expand_in(\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  context: List[ast.Decl],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)]) {\n  derived := derive.derived_in(new, context)\n  folded := derive.folded_in(\n    derived.0,\n    context,\n    (_, _, es) -> es.map(_ -> Err(derive.not_compiled())),\n  )\n  (folded.0, derived.1 + folded.1)\n}","old_text":"/// `expand` of definitions added to a program, with `comptime e` run by\n/// `eval`. `context` (not returned) is what their `derive`s and\n/// `comptime e` read. Expands a program's own definitions without std's.\npub fn expand_in(\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  context: List[ast.Decl],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)]) {\n  derived := derive.derived_in(new, context)\n  folded := derive.folded_in(\n    derived.0,\n    context,\n    (ds, m, es) -> es.map(e -> Err(derive.not_compiled())),\n  )\n  (folded.0, derived.1 + folded.1)\n}"}]}
{"id":"099862180791281c","time":1795657014,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"closure_keys","kind":"fn","old":"661bbcd95f27f61e","new":"1398e06856cfe94e","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"","text":"/// For each definition `verify` checks, a key of it and everything of the\n/// program it depends on, transitively: the code hashes and dependencies\n/// the module files' headers list. By `fn:NAME` (qualified) and `impl:K`\n/// (the program's `K`-th implementation).\nfn closure_keys(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  sources: List[(String, String)],\n) -> Dict[String, String] {\n  keys_over(\n    disk,\n    sources,\n    (_: String, e: binary.Entry) -> bytes_hex(e.code_hash),\n    None,\n    false,\n  )\n}","old_text":"/// For each definition `verify` checks, a key of it and everything of the\n/// program it depends on, transitively: the code hashes and dependencies\n/// the module files' headers list. By `fn:NAME` (qualified) and `impl:K`\n/// (the program's `K`-th implementation).\nfn closure_keys(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  sources: List[(String, String)],\n) -> Dict[String, String] {\n  keys_over(\n    disk,\n    sources,\n    (q: String, e: binary.Entry) -> bytes_hex(e.code_hash),\n    None,\n    false,\n  )\n}"},{"name":"call_command","kind":"fn","old":"bb05d54a918d8a01","new":"dd1352c17c1ac6d0","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"","text":"/// `strata run f ARGS` on the program at `path`.\n/// - The arguments are written as code (`\"abc\", 3`, `Circle { radius: 2\n/// }`) in a function of `f`'s module that calls `f` and shows the result as\n/// the code that writes it (`strata_run_call`).\n/// - It is checked with the program: a wrong argument is invalid input,\n/// exit 2.\n/// - It is compiled by compiler/codegen and run by the JIT (`jit --call`):\n/// prints what it printed and its result, or its fault (exit 1).\nfn call_command(\n  mut console: std.io.Console,\n  mut disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  process: std.process.Process,\n  mut launcher: std.process.Launcher,\n  cache: cache.Cache,\n  line: driver.Args,\n  cwd: String,\n  path: String,\n  lib: Option[driver.StdLibrary],\n  rest: List[String],\n) -> std.process.ExitCode {\n  name := get(rest, 0) ?? \"\"\n  raw := get(rest, 1) ?? \"\"\n  core := shared(disk, cache).core\n  (as_written, own, context) := if disk.exists(path + \"/strata.toml\") {\n    match load_package(\n      mut launcher,\n      mut disk,\n      cache,\n      \"std\",\n      path,\n      false,\n      core,\n    ) {\n      Ok(p) => (p.written, p.own, p.context),\n      Err(e) => return fail_with(mut console, e),\n    }\n  } else {\n    ds := decls_of(disk, path)\n    lib_ds := std_imports(disk, \"std\", ds)\n    (resolve.written(ds, lib_ds, core), ds, lib_ds)\n  }\n  mut found := None\n  for d in own {\n    match d.kind {\n      ast.FnDef(g) => if qualified_name(d.module, g.name) == name {\n        found = Some((d.module, g))\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  (module, f) := match found {\n    Some(x) => x,\n    None => return fail_with(mut console, f\"no function `{name}`\"),\n  }\n  if f.type_params != [] {\n    return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      f\"`{name}` is generic: call it from a function that says which types it is used at\",\n    )\n  }\n  given_args := match parse.parse_expr(\"f(\" + raw + \")\") {\n    Ok(ast.Call { callee: _, args }) => args,\n    Ok(_) => return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      \"the arguments: expected values separated by commas\",\n    ),\n    Err(e) => return fail_with(mut console, \"the arguments: \" + e),\n  }\n  if len(given_args) != len(f.params) {\n    return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      f\"`{name}` takes {len(f.params)} arguments\",\n    )\n  }\n  // a variant's type (`e: TooBig`) given another variant of its sum\n  // (`NonEmptyErr`) takes the sum's value\n  for (p, x) in zip(f.params, given_args) {\n    match (p.ty, x) {\n      (ast.Named { name: want, args: [] }, ast.CtorExpr { name: c, .. }) => match (variant_owner(own, want), variant_owner(own, c)) {\n        (Some(o), Some(o2)) => if o == o2 && want != c {\n          return fail_with(\n            mut console,\n            f\"argument `{p.name}`: expected `{want}`, found `{o}`\",\n          )\n        },\n        _ => (),\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  sized := [\"I8\", \"I16\", \"I32\", \"I64\", \"U8\", \"U16\", \"U32\", \"U64\"]\n  mut stmts := []\n  mut call_args := []\n  for (i, (p, x)) in enumerate(zip(f.params, given_args)) {\n    n := f\"strata_arg_{i}\"\n    if p.mutable {\n      mut stmts.push(ast.VarDecl { name: n, ty: Some(p.ty), value: x })\n      mut call_args.push(ast.MutExpr(ast.Var(n)))\n    } else {\n      // (a sized integer's type is given, so a literal is one)\n      ty := match p.ty {\n        ast.Named { name: t, args: [] } => if contains(sized, t) {\n          Some(p.ty)\n        } else {\n          None\n        },\n        _ => None,\n      }\n      mut stmts.push(ast.Let { pat: ast.Bind(n), ty, value: x })\n      mut call_args.push(ast.Var(n))\n    }\n  }\n  probe := ast.Decl {\n    comments: [],\n    doc: [],\n    module,\n    public: false,\n    kind: ast.FnDef(ast.FnDecl {\n      doc: [],\n      comments: [],\n      name: \"strata_run_call\",\n      type_params: [],\n      bounds: [],\n      params: [],\n      ret: ast.Named { name: \"String\", args: [] },\n      pre: [],\n      post: [],\n      terminating: false,\n      body: ast.Block {\n        stmts,\n        last: ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(\"debug\"), args: [ast.Call {\n          callee: ast.Var(last_segment(name)),\n          args: call_args,\n        }] },\n      },\n      compile_time: false,\n      derived: false,\n    }),\n  }\n  // stored (references qualified) in the module's scope\n  made := match resolve.stored(as_written + [probe], context, core).filter(\n    d ->\n      d.module == module\n        && desugar.decl_name(d) == \"strata_run_call\",\n  ) {\n    [d, ..] => d,\n    _ => return fail_with(mut console, \"the arguments: can't be read\"),\n  }\n  for e in check_errors_of(own + [made], context, core, false) {\n    if ends_with(e.0, \"strata_run_call\") {\n      return fail_with(mut console, \"invalid input: \" + e.1)\n    }\n  }\n  scratch := scratch_of(mut disk, cache, \"run\")\n  call_file := scratch + \"/call.strata\"\n  proofs := scratch + \"/proofs.txt\"\n  not_covered := scratch + \"/errors.txt\"\n  match mut disk.write_bytes(\n    call_file,\n    binary.encode_module(\n      [made],\n      module,\n      Dict[String, List[String]] {},\n    ),\n  ) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  match mut disk.write(proofs, \"\") {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  loads := match lib {\n    Some(l) => [\"--load\", l.shared],\n    None => [],\n  }\n  pre := match lib {\n    Some(l) => [\"--precompiled\", l.names],\n    None => [],\n  }\n  trace := if driver.given(line, \"--trace\") {\n    [\"--trace\"]\n  } else {\n    []\n  }\n  code := jit_file(mut disk, cache, loads\n    + [\n      \"--name\",\n      \"main\",\n      \"--errors\",\n      not_covered,\n      \"--fun\",\n      name,\n      \"--dir\",\n      cwd,\n      \"--scratch\",\n      scratch,\n      \"--proofs\",\n      proofs,\n    ]\n    + pre\n    + trace\n    + [\"--call\", call_file, path])\n  uncovered := match disk.read(not_covered) {\n    Ok(t) => [l for l in lines(t) where starts_with(l, \"error:\")],\n    Err(_) => [],\n  }\n  match mut disk.remove_all(scratch) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  if code == 3 && uncovered != [] {\n    return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      \"compiler/codegen doesn't cover this call yet:\\n\"\n        + placed(\n          disk,\n          process,\n          path,\n          uncovered,\n          console.paint(std.term.Errors),\n        ),\n    )\n  }\n  code\n}","old_text":"/// `strata run f ARGS` on the program at `path`.\n/// - The arguments are written as code (`\"abc\", 3`, `Circle { radius: 2\n/// }`) in a function of `f`'s module that calls `f` and shows the result as\n/// the code that writes it (`strata_run_call`).\n/// - It is checked with the program: a wrong argument is invalid input,\n/// exit 2.\n/// - It is compiled by compiler/codegen and run by the JIT (`jit --call`):\n/// prints what it printed and its result, or its fault (exit 1).\nfn call_command(\n  mut console: std.io.Console,\n  mut disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  process: std.process.Process,\n  mut launcher: std.process.Launcher,\n  cache: cache.Cache,\n  line: driver.Args,\n  cwd: String,\n  path: String,\n  lib: Option[driver.StdLibrary],\n  rest: List[String],\n) -> std.process.ExitCode {\n  name := get(rest, 0) ?? \"\"\n  raw := get(rest, 1) ?? \"\"\n  core := shared(disk, cache).core\n  (as_written, own, context) := if disk.exists(path + \"/strata.toml\") {\n    match load_package(\n      mut launcher,\n      mut disk,\n      cache,\n      \"std\",\n      path,\n      false,\n      core,\n    ) {\n      Ok(p) => (p.written, p.own, p.context),\n      Err(e) => return fail_with(mut console, e),\n    }\n  } else {\n    ds := decls_of(disk, path)\n    lib_ds := std_imports(disk, \"std\", ds)\n    (resolve.written(ds, lib_ds, core), ds, lib_ds)\n  }\n  mut found := None\n  for d in own {\n    match d.kind {\n      ast.FnDef(g) => if qualified_name(d.module, g.name) == name {\n        found = Some((d.module, g))\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  (module, f) := match found {\n    Some(x) => x,\n    None => return fail_with(mut console, f\"no function `{name}`\"),\n  }\n  if f.type_params != [] {\n    return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      f\"`{name}` is generic: call it from a function that says which types it is used at\",\n    )\n  }\n  given_args := match parse.parse_expr(\"f(\" + raw + \")\") {\n    Ok(ast.Call { callee: _, args }) => args,\n    Ok(_) => return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      \"the arguments: expected values separated by commas\",\n    ),\n    Err(e) => return fail_with(mut console, \"the arguments: \" + e),\n  }\n  if len(given_args) != len(f.params) {\n    return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      f\"`{name}` takes {len(f.params)} arguments\",\n    )\n  }\n  // a variant's type (`e: TooBig`) given another variant of its sum\n  // (`NonEmptyErr`) takes the sum's value\n  for (p, x) in zip(f.params, given_args) {\n    match (p.ty, x) {\n      (ast.Named { name: want, args: [] }, ast.CtorExpr { name: c, .. }) => match (variant_owner(own, want), variant_owner(own, c)) {\n        (Some(o), Some(o2)) => if o == o2 && want != c {\n          return fail_with(\n            mut console,\n            f\"argument `{p.name}`: expected `{want}`, found `{o}`\",\n          )\n        },\n        _ => (),\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  sized := [\"I8\", \"I16\", \"I32\", \"I64\", \"U8\", \"U16\", \"U32\", \"U64\"]\n  mut stmts := []\n  mut call_args := []\n  for (i, (p, x)) in enumerate(zip(f.params, given_args)) {\n    n := f\"strata_arg_{i}\"\n    if p.mutable {\n      mut stmts.push(ast.VarDecl { name: n, ty: Some(p.ty), value: x })\n      mut call_args.push(ast.MutExpr(ast.Var(n)))\n    } else {\n      // (a sized integer's type is given, so a literal is one)\n      ty := match p.ty {\n        ast.Named { name: t, args: [] } => if contains(sized, t) {\n          Some(p.ty)\n        } else {\n          None\n        },\n        _ => None,\n      }\n      mut stmts.push(ast.Let { pat: ast.Bind(n), ty, value: x })\n      mut call_args.push(ast.Var(n))\n    }\n  }\n  probe := ast.Decl {\n    comments: [],\n    doc: [],\n    module,\n    public: false,\n    kind: ast.FnDef(ast.FnDecl {\n      doc: [],\n      comments: [],\n      name: \"strata_run_call\",\n      type_params: [],\n      bounds: [],\n      params: [],\n      ret: ast.Named { name: \"String\", args: [] },\n      pre: [],\n      post: [],\n      terminating: false,\n      body: ast.Block {\n        stmts,\n        last: ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(\"debug\"), args: [ast.Call {\n          callee: ast.Var(last_segment(name)),\n          args: call_args,\n        }] },\n      },\n      compile_time: false,\n      derived: false,\n    }),\n  }\n  // stored (references qualified) in the module's scope\n  made := match resolve.stored(as_written + [probe], context, core).filter(\n    d ->\n      d.module == module\n        && desugar.decl_name(d) == \"strata_run_call\",\n  ) {\n    [d, ..more] => d,\n    _ => return fail_with(mut console, \"the arguments: can't be read\"),\n  }\n  for e in check_errors_of(own + [made], context, core, false) {\n    if ends_with(e.0, \"strata_run_call\") {\n      return fail_with(mut console, \"invalid input: \" + e.1)\n    }\n  }\n  scratch := scratch_of(mut disk, cache, \"run\")\n  call_file := scratch + \"/call.strata\"\n  proofs := scratch + \"/proofs.txt\"\n  not_covered := scratch + \"/errors.txt\"\n  match mut disk.write_bytes(\n    call_file,\n    binary.encode_module(\n      [made],\n      module,\n      Dict[String, List[String]] {},\n    ),\n  ) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  match mut disk.write(proofs, \"\") {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  loads := match lib {\n    Some(l) => [\"--load\", l.shared],\n    None => [],\n  }\n  pre := match lib {\n    Some(l) => [\"--precompiled\", l.names],\n    None => [],\n  }\n  trace := if driver.given(line, \"--trace\") {\n    [\"--trace\"]\n  } else {\n    []\n  }\n  code := jit_file(mut disk, cache, loads\n    + [\n      \"--name\",\n      \"main\",\n      \"--errors\",\n      not_covered,\n      \"--fun\",\n      name,\n      \"--dir\",\n      cwd,\n      \"--scratch\",\n      scratch,\n      \"--proofs\",\n      proofs,\n    ]\n    + pre\n    + trace\n    + [\"--call\", call_file, path])\n  uncovered := match disk.read(not_covered) {\n    Ok(t) => [l for l in lines(t) where starts_with(l, \"error:\")],\n    Err(_) => [],\n  }\n  match mut disk.remove_all(scratch) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  if code == 3 && uncovered != [] {\n    return fail_with(\n      mut console,\n      \"compiler/codegen doesn't cover this call yet:\\n\"\n        + placed(\n          disk,\n          process,\n          path,\n          uncovered,\n          console.paint(std.term.Errors),\n        ),\n    )\n  }\n  code\n}"},{"name":"verify_command","kind":"fn","old":"5c3fc578591d6156","new":"03b3c0595933083e","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"","text":"/// `strata verify [SELECTION]` on the script or package (`--file`, else the\n/// package here), with std precompiled loaded; the selection as `--only`.\n/// `--obligations`, `--smt`, `--termination` and `--fuzz` run `smt`, `smt\n/// --queries`, `termination` and `fuzz` instead. Exit 1 on a counterexample\n/// or a broken rule.\nfn verify_command(\n  mut console: std.io.Console,\n  mut disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  process: std.process.Process,\n  mut launcher: std.process.Launcher,\n  cache: cache.Cache,\n  line: driver.Args,\n  cwd: String,\n) -> std.process.ExitCode {\n  given_path := program_given(disk, line, cwd)\n  file := match given_path {\n    Some(p) => p,\n    None => match target_of(disk, line, cwd) {\n      Ok(f) => f,\n      Err(e) => return fail_with(mut console, e),\n    },\n  }\n  mode := match [m for m in [\"--obligations\", \"--termination\", \"--fuzz\", \"--smt\"] where driver.given(line, m)] {\n    [m, ..] => m,\n    _ => \"\",\n  }\n  opts := if mode == \"\" {\n    [\"--cases\", \"--seed\", \"--cross-check\", \"--require\"]\n  } else if mode == \"--fuzz\" {\n    [\"--cases\", \"--seed\"]\n  } else {\n    []\n  }\n  mut args := []\n  for o in opts {\n    match driver.option_value(line, o) {\n      Some(x) => {\n        args += [o, x]\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  if mode == \"\" {\n    for f in [\"--checks\", \"--no-cache\", \"--json\", \"--show-searches\"] {\n      if driver.given(line, f) {\n        mut args.push(f)\n      }\n    }\n    args += std_flags(\n      std_library(\n        mut console,\n        mut disk,\n        process,\n        mut launcher,\n        cache,\n      ),\n    )\n  }\n  // (the selection follows the program's path, when it is given)\n  selection := get(line.pos, if given_path is Some {\n    2\n  } else {\n    1\n  }) ?? \"\"\n  if selection != \"\" {\n    args += [\"--only\", selection]\n  }\n  s := toolchain.solver(disk, process)\n  // (core: each of its module files the selection names, on its own)\n  mut code := 0\n  for unit in units_of(disk, file, selection) {\n    one := args + [unit]\n    c := match mode {\n      \"\" => verify_file(\n        mut console,\n        mut launcher,\n        mut disk,\n        cache,\n        s,\n        toolchain.c_compiler(process),\n        one,\n      ),\n      \"--obligations\" => {\n        smt_file(mut launcher, mut disk, cache, s, one)\n        0\n      },\n      \"--smt\" => {\n        smt_file(\n          mut launcher,\n          mut disk,\n          cache,\n          s,\n          [\"--queries\"] + one,\n        )\n        0\n      },\n      \"--termination\" => {\n        termination_file(mut launcher, mut disk, cache, s, one)\n        0\n      },\n      _ => {\n        fuzz_file(disk, cache, one)\n        0\n      },\n    }\n    if c > code {\n      code = c\n    }\n  }\n  code\n}","old_text":"/// `strata verify [SELECTION]` on the script or package (`--file`, else the\n/// package here), with std precompiled loaded; the selection as `--only`.\n/// `--obligations`, `--smt`, `--termination` and `--fuzz` run `smt`, `smt\n/// --queries`, `termination` and `fuzz` instead. Exit 1 on a counterexample\n/// or a broken rule.\nfn verify_command(\n  mut console: std.io.Console,\n  mut disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  process: std.process.Process,\n  mut launcher: std.process.Launcher,\n  cache: cache.Cache,\n  line: driver.Args,\n  cwd: String,\n) -> std.process.ExitCode {\n  given_path := program_given(disk, line, cwd)\n  file := match given_path {\n    Some(p) => p,\n    None => match target_of(disk, line, cwd) {\n      Ok(f) => f,\n      Err(e) => return fail_with(mut console, e),\n    },\n  }\n  mode := match [m for m in [\"--obligations\", \"--termination\", \"--fuzz\", \"--smt\"] where driver.given(line, m)] {\n    [m, ..more] => m,\n    _ => \"\",\n  }\n  opts := if mode == \"\" {\n    [\"--cases\", \"--seed\", \"--cross-check\", \"--require\"]\n  } else if mode == \"--fuzz\" {\n    [\"--cases\", \"--seed\"]\n  } else {\n    []\n  }\n  mut args := []\n  for o in opts {\n    match driver.option_value(line, o) {\n      Some(x) => {\n        args += [o, x]\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  if mode == \"\" {\n    for f in [\"--checks\", \"--no-cache\", \"--json\", \"--show-searches\"] {\n      if driver.given(line, f) {\n        mut args.push(f)\n      }\n    }\n    args += std_flags(\n      std_library(\n        mut console,\n        mut disk,\n        process,\n        mut launcher,\n        cache,\n      ),\n    )\n  }\n  // (the selection follows the program's path, when it is given)\n  selection := get(line.pos, if given_path is Some {\n    2\n  } else {\n    1\n  }) ?? \"\"\n  if selection != \"\" {\n    args += [\"--only\", selection]\n  }\n  s := toolchain.solver(disk, process)\n  // (core: each of its module files the selection names, on its own)\n  mut code := 0\n  for unit in units_of(disk, file, selection) {\n    one := args + [unit]\n    c := match mode {\n      \"\" => verify_file(\n        mut console,\n        mut launcher,\n        mut disk,\n        cache,\n        s,\n        toolchain.c_compiler(process),\n        one,\n      ),\n      \"--obligations\" => {\n        smt_file(mut launcher, mut disk, cache, s, one)\n        0\n      },\n      \"--smt\" => {\n        smt_file(\n          mut launcher,\n          mut disk,\n          cache,\n          s,\n          [\"--queries\"] + one,\n        )\n        0\n      },\n      \"--termination\" => {\n        termination_file(mut launcher, mut disk, cache, s, one)\n        0\n      },\n      _ => {\n        fuzz_file(disk, cache, one)\n        0\n      },\n    }\n    if c > code {\n      code = c\n    }\n  }\n  code\n}"},{"name":"closure_keys_of","kind":"fn","old":"29563d8a630cc7fb","new":"0c18d4211d7ac516","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"","text":"/// Only for the definitions `defs`.\nfn closure_keys_of(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  sources: List[(String, String)],\n  defs: Set[String],\n) -> Dict[String, String] {\n  keys_over(\n    disk,\n    sources,\n    (_: String, e: binary.Entry) -> bytes_hex(e.code_hash),\n    Some(defs),\n    false,\n  )\n}","old_text":"/// Only for the definitions `defs`.\nfn closure_keys_of(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  sources: List[(String, String)],\n  defs: Set[String],\n) -> Dict[String, String] {\n  keys_over(\n    disk,\n    sources,\n    (q: String, e: binary.Entry) -> bytes_hex(e.code_hash),\n    Some(defs),\n    false,\n  )\n}"},{"name":"core_rt_object","kind":"fn","old":"c19e847665954d42","new":"3c7697ecafeac862","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"","text":"/// core.rt's object (compiled by compiler/codegen, then LLVM at -O2),\n/// cached by its IR (`core-rt/KEY.o`, `KEY` its SHA-256 with\n/// `toolchain.object_settings`). Which IR this compiler makes of this core\n/// is cached too (`core-rt-of/KEY`: the sources it was built from,\n/// `maker_key`, and core's and the prelude's code, `sh.stamp`), so a new\n/// compiler compiles it again only when it makes other IR of it. In\n/// `scratch` when nothing is cached.\nfn core_rt_object(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  sh: Shared,\n  scratch: String,\n) -> Result[String, String] {\n  mut d := disk\n  made_of := if sh.stamp == \"\" {\n    \"\"\n  } else {\n    \"core-rt-of/\" + maker_key(\"core-rt\", [sh.stamp])\n  }\n  kept := (key: String) ->\n    cache.find_entry(disk, sh.cache, \"core-rt/\" + key + \".o\")\n  if made_of != \"\" {\n    match cache.read_entry(disk, sh.cache, made_of) {\n      Some(key) => match kept(key) {\n        Some(o) => return Ok(o),\n        None => (),\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  text := codegen_with(disk, sh, [\"--core-rt\"], [])\n  match driver.codegen_errors(text) {\n    [e, ..] => return Err(\"compiler/codegen can't compile core.rt: \" + e),\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  if made_of == \"\" {\n    o := scratch + \"/core_rt.o\"\n    return match toolchain.object(mut d, text, o, 2) {\n      Ok(_) => Ok(o),\n      Err(e) => Err(e),\n    }\n  }\n  key := cache.content_key([\n    \"core.rt\",\n    cache.text_sha256_hex(text),\n    toolchain.object_settings(2),\n  ])\n  match kept(key) {\n    Some(o) => {\n      match cache.write_entry(mut d, sh.cache, made_of, key) {\n        _ => (),\n      }\n      return Ok(o)\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  o := cache.own_path(mut d, sh.cache, \"core-rt/\" + key + \".o\")\n  // (to a file of its own, renamed when done: another process may be\n  // making it too)\n  tmp := o + \".\" + f\"{driver_pid().to_int()}\"\n  match toolchain.object(mut d, text, tmp, 2) {\n    Ok(_) => (),\n    Err(e) => return Err(e),\n  }\n  match mut d.rename(tmp, o) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  match cache.write_entry(mut d, sh.cache, made_of, key) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  Ok(o)\n}","old_text":"/// core.rt's object (compiled by compiler/codegen, then LLVM at -O2),\n/// cached by its IR (`core-rt/KEY.o`, `KEY` its SHA-256 with\n/// `toolchain.object_settings`). Which IR this compiler makes of this core\n/// is cached too (`core-rt-of/KEY`: the sources it was built from,\n/// `maker_key`, and core's and the prelude's code, `sh.stamp`), so a new\n/// compiler compiles it again only when it makes other IR of it. In\n/// `scratch` when nothing is cached.\nfn core_rt_object(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  sh: Shared,\n  scratch: String,\n) -> Result[String, String] {\n  mut d := disk\n  made_of := if sh.stamp == \"\" {\n    \"\"\n  } else {\n    \"core-rt-of/\" + maker_key(\"core-rt\", [sh.stamp])\n  }\n  kept := (key: String) ->\n    cache.find_entry(disk, sh.cache, \"core-rt/\" + key + \".o\")\n  if made_of != \"\" {\n    match cache.read_entry(disk, sh.cache, made_of) {\n      Some(key) => match kept(key) {\n        Some(o) => return Ok(o),\n        None => (),\n      },\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  text := codegen_with(disk, sh, [\"--core-rt\"], [])\n  match driver.codegen_errors(text) {\n    [e, ..more] => return Err(\"compiler/codegen can't compile core.rt: \" + e),\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  if made_of == \"\" {\n    o := scratch + \"/core_rt.o\"\n    return match toolchain.object(mut d, text, o, 2) {\n      Ok(_) => Ok(o),\n      Err(e) => Err(e),\n    }\n  }\n  key := cache.content_key([\n    \"core.rt\",\n    cache.text_sha256_hex(text),\n    toolchain.object_settings(2),\n  ])\n  match kept(key) {\n    Some(o) => {\n      match cache.write_entry(mut d, sh.cache, made_of, key) {\n        _ => (),\n      }\n      return Ok(o)\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  o := cache.own_path(mut d, sh.cache, \"core-rt/\" + key + \".o\")\n  // (to a file of its own, renamed when done: another process may be\n  // making it too)\n  tmp := o + \".\" + f\"{driver_pid().to_int()}\"\n  match toolchain.object(mut d, text, tmp, 2) {\n    Ok(_) => (),\n    Err(e) => return Err(e),\n  }\n  match mut d.rename(tmp, o) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  match cache.write_entry(mut d, sh.cache, made_of, key) {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  Ok(o)\n}"},{"name":"verified_decls","kind":"fn","old":"2530bfb2064650ae","new":"39f740e565ff0548","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"","text":"/// `verified_with` for the definitions `ds`, as stored (a version of the\n/// program `files` held, for `strata diff --graph`). std is read from\n/// `dir`, the settings from `files`.\nfn verified_decls(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  dir: String,\n  files: List[String],\n  ds: List[ast.Decl],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], Dict[String, ast.FnDecl], Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl], List[smt.BuiltinSig], smt.Methods) {\n  (sweet0, _) := desugar.desugar(ds)\n  // std as far as the program reaches it (`std_reached`), without the\n  // modules checked\n  // (with the package's settings: `[json] integers = \"proven\"`)\n  mut settings := Dict[String, String] {}\n  for f in files {\n    settings = settings_at(disk, f)\n  }\n  (lib, _) := desugar.desugar(\n    derive.with_settings(std_reached(disk, dir, ds), settings),\n  )\n  // each `derive` as the `impl` it makes, with the copies of the trait's\n  // module's functions made for it (`std.json.encode_as.for.Color.1`)\n  derives := sweet0.any(d -> is_derive(d))\n  // (each call spreading records written out: `f(...x)` is `f(x.a, x.b)`)\n  sweet := check.spreads_resolved(if derives {\n    derive.expand_in(sweet0, lib).0\n  } else {\n    sweet0\n  }, lib, read_core(disk)).0\n  core := module_decls(disk, core_files())\n  (fns, types) := smt.tables(core + lib + sweet)\n  sigs := smt.builtins_of(core)\n  methods := smt.methods_of(core + lib + sweet)\n  // method calls resolved to their trait (`Trait::m`), each lambda's\n  // parameter typed as the checker infers it\n  // (a type's own methods called by name, the receiver's type as the\n  // checker infers it: `app().handle(req)` is `Router.handle`'s)\n  own := smt.elaborated(check.own_methods_resolved(\n    check.lambdas_typed(sweet, lib, read_core(disk)),\n    lib,\n    read_core(disk),\n  ), methods, fns, sigs)\n  (fns0, types) := smt.tables(core + smt.elaborated(lib, methods, fns, sigs) + own)\n  // a C function (`extern c`) is called by its contract, never seen\n  // through: its body is a hole, so it can't be shown to finish without\n  // failing, nor can what calls it\n  mut fns := fns0\n  for d in core + lib + sweet {\n    match d.kind {\n      ast.ExternDef(ast.ExternDecl { lang: ast.C, item: ast.ExternFn(f) }) => {\n        q := if d.module == \"\" {\n          f.name\n        } else {\n          d.module + \".\" + f.name\n        }\n        mut fns.insert(\n          q,\n          ast.FnDecl { ..f, body: ast.Hole(\"extern c\") },\n        )\n      },\n      // (an `extern python` one too)\n      ast.FnDef(f) => if desugar.python_call(f) {\n        mut fns.insert(\n          if d.module == \"\" {\n            f.name\n          } else {\n            d.module + \".\" + f.name\n          },\n          ast.FnDecl { ..f, body: ast.Hole(\"extern python\") },\n        )\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  (own, fns, types, sigs, methods)\n}","old_text":"/// `verified_with` for the definitions `ds`, as stored (a version of the\n/// program `files` held, for `strata diff --graph`). std is read from\n/// `dir`, the settings from `files`.\nfn verified_decls(\n  disk: std.fs.Disk,\n  dir: String,\n  files: List[String],\n  ds: List[ast.Decl],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], Dict[String, ast.FnDecl], Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl], List[smt.BuiltinSig], smt.Methods) {\n  (sweet0, _) := desugar.desugar(ds)\n  // std as far as the program reaches it (`std_reached`), without the\n  // modules checked\n  own_modules := set(ds.map(d -> d.module))\n  // (with the package's settings: `[json] integers = \"proven\"`)\n  mut settings := Dict[String, String] {}\n  for f in files {\n    settings = settings_at(disk, f)\n  }\n  (lib, _) := desugar.desugar(\n    derive.with_settings(std_reached(disk, dir, ds), settings),\n  )\n  // each `derive` as the `impl` it makes, with the copies of the trait's\n  // module's functions made for it (`std.json.encode_as.for.Color.1`)\n  derives := sweet0.any(d -> is_derive(d))\n  // (each call spreading records written out: `f(...x)` is `f(x.a, x.b)`)\n  sweet := check.spreads_resolved(if derives {\n    derive.expand_in(sweet0, lib).0\n  } else {\n    sweet0\n  }, lib, read_core(disk)).0\n  core := module_decls(disk, core_files())\n  (fns, types) := smt.tables(core + lib + sweet)\n  sigs := smt.builtins_of(core)\n  methods := smt.methods_of(core + lib + sweet)\n  // method calls resolved to their trait (`Trait::m`), each lambda's\n  // parameter typed as the checker infers it\n  // (a type's own methods called by name, the receiver's type as the\n  // checker infers it: `app().handle(req)` is `Router.handle`'s)\n  own := smt.elaborated(check.own_methods_resolved(\n    check.lambdas_typed(sweet, lib, read_core(disk)),\n    lib,\n    read_core(disk),\n  ), methods, fns, sigs)\n  (fns0, types) := smt.tables(core + smt.elaborated(lib, methods, fns, sigs) + own)\n  // a C function (`extern c`) is called by its contract, never seen\n  // through: its body is a hole, so it can't be shown to finish without\n  // failing, nor can what calls it\n  mut fns := fns0\n  for d in core + lib + sweet {\n    match d.kind {\n      ast.ExternDef(ast.ExternDecl { lang: ast.C, item: ast.ExternFn(f) }) => {\n        q := if d.module == \"\" {\n          f.name\n        } else {\n          d.module + \".\" + f.name\n        }\n        mut fns.insert(\n          q,\n          ast.FnDecl { ..f, body: ast.Hole(\"extern c\") },\n        )\n      },\n      // (an `extern python` one too)\n      ast.FnDef(f) => if desugar.python_call(f) {\n        mut fns.insert(\n          if d.module == \"\" {\n            f.name\n          } else {\n            d.module + \".\" + f.name\n          },\n          ast.FnDecl { ..f, body: ast.Hole(\"extern python\") },\n        )\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  (own, fns, types, sigs, methods)\n}"}]}
{"id":"a751f2a73e13b348","time":1795657065,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"pending.variants_of","kind":"fn","old":"77da8f3298754728","new":"8fd504db89768782","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"pending","text":"/// Each variant with the pattern that matches it (`Locked`, `Locked(_)`,\n/// `Locked { .. }`).\nfn variants_of(ds: List[ast.Decl], q: String) -> List[(String, ast.Pattern)] {\n  match pending.find_decl(ds, q) {\n    Some(d) => match d.kind {\n      ast.TypeDef(t) => match t.body {\n        ast.SumBody(vs) => vs.map(\n          v -> (\n            v.name,\n            ast.CtorPattern { name: v.name, args: match v.payload {\n              ast.NoPayload => ast.NoPats,\n              ast.Positional(ts) => ast.PositionalPats(ts.map(_ -> ast.Wild)),\n              ast.RecordPayload(_) => ast.RecordPats { fields: [], rest: true },\n              ast.MemberType(_) => ast.NoPats,\n            } },\n          ),\n        ),\n        _ => [],\n      },\n      _ => [],\n    },\n    None => [],\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// Each variant with the pattern that matches it (`Locked`, `Locked(_)`,\n/// `Locked { .. }`).\nfn variants_of(ds: List[ast.Decl], q: String) -> List[(String, ast.Pattern)] {\n  match pending.find_decl(ds, q) {\n    Some(d) => match d.kind {\n      ast.TypeDef(t) => match t.body {\n        ast.SumBody(vs) => vs.map(\n          v -> (\n            v.name,\n            ast.CtorPattern { name: v.name, args: match v.payload {\n              ast.NoPayload => ast.NoPats,\n              ast.Positional(ts) => ast.PositionalPats(ts.map(x -> ast.Wild)),\n              ast.RecordPayload(_) => ast.RecordPats { fields: [], rest: true },\n              ast.MemberType(_) => ast.NoPats,\n            } },\n          ),\n        ),\n        _ => [],\n      },\n      _ => [],\n    },\n    None => [],\n  }\n}"}]}
{"id":"63c46f65d0a78e55","time":1795657066,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"smt.encode_rounds","kind":"fn","old":"d71c3b56027e05fe","new":"daeb34f81a496871","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"smt","text":"/// `encode` of each of `fs` (each with its label), in order. The questions\n/// they all ask in a round are asked together (`run_scripts`), each\n/// distinct one once. Gives the same encodings as one by one.\nfn encode_rounds(\n  mut commands: std.process.Commands,\n  mut files: std.fs.Files,\n  scratch: String,\n  solver: String,\n  fns: Dict[String, ast.FnDecl],\n  types: Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl],\n  sigs: List[smt.BuiltinSig],\n  methods: smt.Methods,\n  fs: List[(ast.FnDecl, String)],\n) -> List[smt.Vc] {\n  mut answers := Dict[String, String] {}\n  mut done: List[Option[smt.Vc]] = fs.map(_ -> None)\n  while true {\n    mut now: List[Option[smt.Vc]] = []\n    mut asked := []\n    for (i, (f, label)) in enumerate(fs) {\n      match get(done, i) ?? None {\n        Some(v) => mut now.push(Some(v)),\n        None => {\n          mut vc := smt.new_vc(fns, types, sigs, methods)\n          vc.answers = answers\n          smt.function(mut vc, f, label)\n          if len(vc.pending) == 0 || len(vc.gaps) > 0 {\n            mut now.push(Some(vc))\n          } else {\n            mut now.push(None)\n            for q in vc.pending {\n              if !contains(asked, q) {\n                mut asked.push(q)\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n      }\n    }\n    done = now\n    if asked == [] {\n      break\n    }\n    timings.begin(\"smt: a round of questions\")\n    outs := smt.run_scripts(\n      mut commands,\n      mut files,\n      scratch,\n      solver,\n      asked.map(\n        q -> (\n          byte_slice(q, index_of(q, \"\\n\") ?? 0, byte_len(q)),\n          smt.question_flags(q),\n        ),\n      ),\n    )\n    timings.end(\"smt: a round of questions\")\n    for (k, q) in enumerate(asked) {\n      mut answers.insert(q, get(get(outs, k) ?? [], 0) ?? \"\")\n    }\n  }\n  done.map(v -> v ?? smt.new_vc(fns, types, sigs, methods))\n}","old_text":"/// `encode` of each of `fs` (each with its label), in order. The questions\n/// they all ask in a round are asked together (`run_scripts`), each\n/// distinct one once. Gives the same encodings as one by one.\nfn encode_rounds(\n  mut commands: std.process.Commands,\n  mut files: std.fs.Files,\n  scratch: String,\n  solver: String,\n  fns: Dict[String, ast.FnDecl],\n  types: Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl],\n  sigs: List[smt.BuiltinSig],\n  methods: smt.Methods,\n  fs: List[(ast.FnDecl, String)],\n) -> List[smt.Vc] {\n  mut answers := Dict[String, String] {}\n  mut done: List[Option[smt.Vc]] = fs.map(x -> None)\n  while true {\n    mut now: List[Option[smt.Vc]] = []\n    mut asked := []\n    for (i, (f, label)) in enumerate(fs) {\n      match get(done, i) ?? None {\n        Some(v) => mut now.push(Some(v)),\n        None => {\n          mut vc := smt.new_vc(fns, types, sigs, methods)\n          vc.answers = answers\n          smt.function(mut vc, f, label)\n          if len(vc.pending) == 0 || len(vc.gaps) > 0 {\n            mut now.push(Some(vc))\n          } else {\n            mut now.push(None)\n            for q in vc.pending {\n              if !contains(asked, q) {\n                mut asked.push(q)\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n      }\n    }\n    done = now\n    if asked == [] {\n      break\n    }\n    timings.begin(\"smt: a round of questions\")\n    outs := smt.run_scripts(\n      mut commands,\n      mut files,\n      scratch,\n      solver,\n      asked.map(\n        q -> (\n          byte_slice(q, index_of(q, \"\\n\") ?? 0, byte_len(q)),\n          smt.question_flags(q),\n        ),\n      ),\n    )\n    timings.end(\"smt: a round of questions\")\n    for (k, q) in enumerate(asked) {\n      mut answers.insert(q, get(get(outs, k) ?? [], 0) ?? \"\")\n    }\n  }\n  done.map(v -> v ?? smt.new_vc(fns, types, sigs, methods))\n}"}]}
{"id":"1a3125bcffa7396c","time":1795657082,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"termination.analyze","kind":"fn","old":"c29c6ecbfc8c654f","new":"3ebbb1dc50d93e23","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// The termination verdict of every function and implementation method\n/// (`roots: None`), or of those `roots` reach plus the helpers refinements\n/// call. The others are left unknown, and none of them is transparent.\npub fn analyze(\n  mut commands: std.process.Commands,\n  mut files: std.fs.Files,\n  ctx: termination.Ctx,\n  roots: Option[Set[String]],\n) -> termination.Analysis {\n  termination.analyze_with(\n    mut commands,\n    mut files,\n    ctx,\n    roots,\n    _ -> None,\n    _ -> None,\n  ).0\n}","old_text":"/// The termination verdict of every function and implementation method\n/// (`roots: None`), or of those `roots` reach plus the helpers refinements\n/// call. The others are left unknown, and none of them is transparent.\npub fn analyze(\n  mut commands: std.process.Commands,\n  mut files: std.fs.Files,\n  ctx: termination.Ctx,\n  roots: Option[Set[String]],\n) -> termination.Analysis {\n  termination.analyze_with(\n    mut commands,\n    mut files,\n    ctx,\n    roots,\n    n -> None,\n    n -> None,\n  ).0\n}"}]}
{"id":"0e6253cf4c4993ca","time":1795657247,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"codegen.apply","kind":"fn","old":"f4ddd41d83277abe","new":"be16bf17c3e08061","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"codegen","text":"fn apply(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  op: ast.BinOp,\n  a0: codegen.V,\n  b0: codegen.V,\n) -> codegen.V {\n  // an integer literal next to a sized integer takes its type\n  a := codegen.as_type(mut g, a0, b0.ty)\n  b := codegen.as_type(mut g, b0, a0.ty)\n  match codegen.sized(a.ty) {\n    Some(w) => match op {\n      ast.Equal | ast.NotEqual => (),\n      _ => return codegen.word_op(mut g, op, w, a, b),\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  match op {\n    ast.Equal => return codegen.equal(mut g, a, b),\n    ast.NotEqual => {\n      e := codegen.equal(mut g, a, b)\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"ne\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = xor i1 {e.op}, true\")\n      return codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: r }\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  match a.ty {\n    check.TInt => match op {\n      ast.Add => codegen.int_op(mut g, \"sadd\", a, b),\n      ast.Sub => codegen.int_op(mut g, \"ssub\", a, b),\n      ast.Mul => codegen.int_op(mut g, \"smul\", a, b),\n      // proven nonzero: the runtime division without its zero check\n      ast.Div | ast.Mod => {\n        nz := if codegen.proven(mut g, \"no division by zero\", \"exact\") {\n          \"_nz\"\n        } else {\n          \"\"\n        }\n        f := if op is ast.Div {\n          \"strata_div\"\n        } else {\n          \"strata_mod\"\n        }\n        codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, f + nz, [a, b])\n      },\n      ast.BitAnd => codegen.bit_op(mut g, \"and\", a, b),\n      ast.BitOr => codegen.bit_op(mut g, \"or\", a, b),\n      ast.BitXor => codegen.bit_op(mut g, \"xor\", a, b),\n      ast.Shl => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_shl\", [a, b]),\n      ast.Shr => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_shr\", [a, b]),\n      ast.Less => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"slt\", a, b),\n      ast.LessEq => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"sle\", a, b),\n      ast.Greater => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"sgt\", a, b),\n      ast.GreaterEq => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"sge\", a, b),\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op),\n    },\n    check.TFloat => match op {\n      ast.Add | ast.Sub | ast.Mul | ast.Div => {\n        ins := match op {\n          ast.Add => \"fadd\",\n          ast.Sub => \"fsub\",\n          ast.Mul => \"fmul\",\n          _ => \"fdiv\",\n        }\n        r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"f\")\n        codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = {ins} double {a.op}, {b.op}\")\n        codegen.finite(\n          mut g,\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: r },\n          a,\n          b,\n          op,\n        )\n      },\n      ast.Mod => {\n        r := codegen.call(mut g, check.TFloat, \"strata_fmod\", [a, b])\n        codegen.finite(mut g, r, a, b, op)\n      },\n      ast.Less => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp olt\", a, b),\n      ast.LessEq => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp ole\", a, b),\n      ast.Greater => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp ogt\", a, b),\n      ast.GreaterEq => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp oge\", a, b),\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op),\n    },\n    check.TStr => match op {\n      ast.Add => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_concat\", [a, b]),\n      // code point order, which UTF-8 byte order preserves (`strata_str_cmp`)\n      ast.Less | ast.LessEq | ast.Greater | ast.GreaterEq => {\n        codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_str_cmp\")\n        c := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"sc\")\n        codegen.emit(\n          mut g,\n          f\"{c} = call i64 @strata_str_cmp(ptr {a.op}, ptr {b.op})\",\n        )\n        pred := match op {\n          ast.Less => \"slt\",\n          ast.LessEq => \"sle\",\n          ast.Greater => \"sgt\",\n          _ => \"sge\",\n        }\n        codegen.compare(\n          mut g,\n          \"icmp \" + pred,\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: c },\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: \"0\" },\n        )\n      },\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op),\n    },\n    check.TList(et) => match op {\n      ast.Add => {\n        t := codegen.better(a.ty, b.ty)\n        k := codegen.elements_kind(match t {\n          check.TList(x) => x,\n          _ => et,\n        })\n        codegen.call(mut g, t, \"strata_list_concat\", [a, b, k])\n      },\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op),\n    },\n    _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op),\n  }\n}","old_text":"fn apply(\n  mut g: codegen.Gen,\n  op: ast.BinOp,\n  a0: codegen.V,\n  b0: codegen.V,\n) -> codegen.V {\n  // an integer literal next to a sized integer takes its type\n  a := codegen.as_type(mut g, a0, b0.ty)\n  b := codegen.as_type(mut g, b0, a0.ty)\n  match codegen.sized(a.ty) {\n    Some(w) => match op {\n      ast.Equal | ast.NotEqual => (),\n      _ => return codegen.word_op(mut g, op, w, a, b),\n    },\n    None => (),\n  }\n  match op {\n    ast.Equal => return codegen.equal(mut g, a, b),\n    ast.NotEqual => {\n      e := codegen.equal(mut g, a, b)\n      r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"ne\")\n      codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = xor i1 {e.op}, true\")\n      return codegen.V { ty: check.TBool, op: r }\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  match a.ty {\n    check.TInt => match op {\n      ast.Add => codegen.int_op(mut g, \"sadd\", a, b),\n      ast.Sub => codegen.int_op(mut g, \"ssub\", a, b),\n      ast.Mul => codegen.int_op(mut g, \"smul\", a, b),\n      // proven nonzero: the runtime division without its zero check\n      ast.Div | ast.Mod => {\n        nz := if codegen.proven(mut g, \"no division by zero\", \"exact\") {\n          \"_nz\"\n        } else {\n          \"\"\n        }\n        f := if op is ast.Div {\n          \"strata_div\"\n        } else {\n          \"strata_mod\"\n        }\n        codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, f + nz, [a, b])\n      },\n      ast.BitAnd => codegen.bit_op(mut g, \"and\", a, b),\n      ast.BitOr => codegen.bit_op(mut g, \"or\", a, b),\n      ast.BitXor => codegen.bit_op(mut g, \"xor\", a, b),\n      ast.Shl => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_shl\", [a, b]),\n      ast.Shr => codegen.call(mut g, check.TInt, \"strata_shr\", [a, b]),\n      ast.Less => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"slt\", a, b),\n      ast.LessEq => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"sle\", a, b),\n      ast.Greater => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"sgt\", a, b),\n      ast.GreaterEq => codegen.int_compare(mut g, \"sge\", a, b),\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op, a),\n    },\n    check.TFloat => match op {\n      ast.Add | ast.Sub | ast.Mul | ast.Div => {\n        ins := match op {\n          ast.Add => \"fadd\",\n          ast.Sub => \"fsub\",\n          ast.Mul => \"fmul\",\n          _ => \"fdiv\",\n        }\n        r := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"f\")\n        codegen.emit(mut g, f\"{r} = {ins} double {a.op}, {b.op}\")\n        codegen.finite(\n          mut g,\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TFloat, op: r },\n          a,\n          b,\n          op,\n        )\n      },\n      ast.Mod => {\n        r := codegen.call(mut g, check.TFloat, \"strata_fmod\", [a, b])\n        codegen.finite(mut g, r, a, b, op)\n      },\n      ast.Less => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp olt\", a, b),\n      ast.LessEq => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp ole\", a, b),\n      ast.Greater => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp ogt\", a, b),\n      ast.GreaterEq => codegen.compare(mut g, \"fcmp oge\", a, b),\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op, a),\n    },\n    check.TStr => match op {\n      ast.Add => codegen.call(mut g, check.TStr, \"strata_concat\", [a, b]),\n      // code point order, which UTF-8 byte order preserves (`strata_str_cmp`)\n      ast.Less | ast.LessEq | ast.Greater | ast.GreaterEq => {\n        codegen.use_rt(mut g, \"strata_str_cmp\")\n        c := codegen.fresh(mut g, \"sc\")\n        codegen.emit(\n          mut g,\n          f\"{c} = call i64 @strata_str_cmp(ptr {a.op}, ptr {b.op})\",\n        )\n        pred := match op {\n          ast.Less => \"slt\",\n          ast.LessEq => \"sle\",\n          ast.Greater => \"sgt\",\n          _ => \"sge\",\n        }\n        codegen.compare(\n          mut g,\n          \"icmp \" + pred,\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: c },\n          codegen.V { ty: check.TInt, op: \"0\" },\n        )\n      },\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op, a),\n    },\n    check.TList(et) => match op {\n      ast.Add => {\n        t := codegen.better(a.ty, b.ty)\n        k := codegen.elements_kind(match t {\n          check.TList(x) => x,\n          _ => et,\n        })\n        codegen.call(mut g, t, \"strata_list_concat\", [a, b, k])\n      },\n      _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op, a),\n    },\n    _ => codegen.bad_op(mut g, op, a),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"codegen.bad_op","kind":"fn","old":"e5f93db7cd2a964b","new":"187a0a82275f649a","interface_changed":true,"affected":["codegen.apply","codegen.equal","codegen.word_op","codegen.binary","codegen.number_builtin","codegen.checked","codegen.eq_fields","codegen.matches","codegen.eq_list","codegen.dyn_wrapper","codegen.union_eq","codegen.slot_fn","codegen.expr_node","codegen.builtin","codegen.assertion","codegen.invariants","codegen.eq_body","codegen.destructure","codegen.binds","codegen.for_loop","codegen.matching_v","codegen.match_got","codegen.helper","codegen.vtable","codegen.cmp_helper","codegen.table_fns","codegen.hash_helper","codegen.expr","codegen.call_named","codegen.builtin_call","codegen.push_in_place","codegen.stmt_node","codegen.matching_want","codegen.show","codegen.shown","codegen.to_dyn","codegen.dyn_table_is","codegen.order_closure","codegen.cmp_fields","codegen.union_cmp","codegen.compare_values","codegen.collection_builtin","codegen.update_in_place","codegen.table_from","codegen.hash_fields","codegen.interp","codegen.logic","codegen.get_field","codegen.loop_body","codegen.method_call","codegen.except_expr","codegen.with_it","codegen.check_requires","codegen.check_ensures","codegen.for_list","codegen.main_arg","codegen.await_expr","codegen.select_